nters: the 13 pass-five `kill-switch-cli` files listed in `review/review-scope-5.txt`, plus the shared docs that describe them (`INSTALL-GUIDE.md`, `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`, `changelog/v1.1.0.0.md`, `.skilled/hooks/README.md`) and the pass-four lineage context.\n213: - Behavior claims to verify: `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED` and its aliases plus `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED` make a direct `advisor_recommend` call abstain before any daemon starts or the scorer runs; the launcher passes no switch name to a daemon it starts; a flags-file entry disables the caller; a caller's `0` beats the file; the disabled envelope carries empty recommendations, `freshness: unavailable`, `ADVISOR_DISABLED` and no prompt text.\n214: - Reuse and conventions: `hook-flags.cjs` is the single resolver (`MASTER_FLAG`, `MASTER_ALIASES`, `LEGACY_ALIASES`, `concernFlag`, `hookFlagDecision`); `advisor-disabled.ts` is the shared envelope builder; `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` is the caller-side strip list.\n215: - Review risks and gaps: the pass-five scope is a changed-file list, not a module map; `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` and the Python shim are out of scope even though they touch the switch; the coverage graph is unavailable, so STOP is graphless.\n216: \n217: ---\n218: \n219: ## 13. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n220: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\n221: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n222: |----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n223: | `spec_code` | core | pending | - | kill-switch claims vs resolver and CLI/handler |\n224: | `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | pass-five brief checks against reviewed files |\n225: | `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | - | no agent definition changed in this area |\n226: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | - | no runtime mirror changed in this area |\n227: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | feature catalog rows that describe the switches |\n228: | `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | CP-003 scenario commands vs the resolver |\n229: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\n230: \n231: ---\n232: \n233: ## 14. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n234: <!-- ANCHOR:files-under-review -->\n235: | File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n236: |------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n237: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts` | - | - | - | pending |\n238: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts` | - | - | - | pending |\n239: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` | - | - | - | pending |\n240: | `.skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs` | - | - | - | pending |\n241: | `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example` | - | - | - | pending |\n242: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md` | - | - | - | pending |\n243: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md` | - | - | - | pending |\n244: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/advisor-disabled.vitest.ts` | - | - | - | pending |\n245: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend.vitest.ts` | - | - | - | pending |\n246: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts` | - | - | - | pending |\n247: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts` | - | - | - | pending |\n248: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-test-utils.ts` | - | - | - | pending |\n249: | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md` | - | - | - | pending |\n250: <!-- /ANCHOR:files-under-review -->\n251: \n252: ---\n253: \n254: ## 15. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n255: <!-- ANCHOR:review-boundaries -->\n256: - Max iterations: 4\n257: - Convergence threshold: 0.10\n258: - Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n259: - No-progress threshold: 0.05\n260: - Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n261: - Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-kill-switch-cli-5-1794760565927-i99t40, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\n262: - Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n263: - Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n264: - Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\n265: - Severity threshold: P2\n266: - Review target type: spec-folder\n267: - Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\n268: - Started: 2026-11-15T16:45:27Z\n269: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-boundaries -->","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-269\n1: # Deep Review Strategy - kill-switch-cli-5 Lineage\n2: \n3: ## 1. REVIEW CHARTER\n4: \n5: - Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder target)\n6: - Fan-out lineage: `kill-switch-cli-5` (artifact dir `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5`); pass-five area is `kill-switch-cli`\n7: - Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability\n8: - Stop conditions: legal convergence at `convergenceThreshold=0.10`, or `maxIterations=4`, whichever comes first\n9: - Success criteria: every pass-five area file reviewed; every finding carries `file:line` and a concrete input; the kill switch and direct-call switch are checked against every path they claim to stop; docs that disagree with code are reported; holdout hygiene is counts-only\n10: - Review focus (operator bound): pass-five code review of command surfacing. Read `review-brief-5.txt` in the packet first and follow it. Review the files whose area is `kill-switch-cli` plus shared docs that describe them. Check the advisor kill switch and the direct-call off switch, the CLI client check, the launcher child-env allowlist, the flags-file resolver, the manual disable scenario, the handler path, the tests that pin the switch, and docs that disagree with code. Never open `command-prompts.jsonl`, `holdout-prompts.jsonl` or `behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl` except through `jq del(.prompt)`, and print counts only.\n11: - Resource map: `resource-map.md` not present; skipping coverage gate\n12: \n13: ---\n14: \n15: ## 2. TOPIC\n16: \n17: Advisor kill-switch and direct-call switch behaviour for the routed skill/command advisor, restricted to the pass-five `kill-switch-cli` area: the shared disable resolver, the CLI client abstain path, the daemon handler abstain path, the launcher child-env filter, the manual disable scenario, the docs that describe the switches, and the tests that pin them.\n18: \n19: ---\n20: \n21: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n22: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n23: [All dimensions complete]\n24: \n25: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n26: \n27: ---\n28: \n29: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n30: \n31: - Not reviewing `vibe-hooks-doctor`, `accuracy-runner` or `docs-metadata` area files except as read-only context when a cross-area contract is required\n32: - Not reviewing `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` (not in the pass-five scope list); command-offer fit is noted only as out-of-scope context\n33: - Not fixing anything: the review is observation-only\n34: - Not reading or printing holdout prompt text; holdout coverage is counts-only\n35: - Not running repo tooling that writes outside the lineage; runners are audited by reading\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n40: \n41: - Legal convergence (all dimensions covered plus stabilization) at or below `convergenceThreshold`\n42: - `maxIterations=4` reached (`stopReason: maxIterationsReached`)\n43: - Any active P0 blocks a PASS verdict but does not stop iteration dispatch by itself; the P0 override keeps `newFindingsRatio >= 0.50`\n44: \n45: ---\n46: \n47: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n48: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n49: - [x] correctness\n50: - [x] security\n51: - [x] traceability\n52: - [x] maintainability\n53: \n54: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n55: \n56: ---\n57: \n58: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n59: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n60: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n61: - P1 (Required): 0\n62: - P2 (Suggestions): 6\n63: - Resolved: 0\n64: \n65: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n66: \n67: ---\n68: \n69: ## 6. WHAT WORKED\n70: - Reading the resolver and both call sites together confirmed the switch decision precedes every daemon and scorer path; the no-daemon test pins the CLI half (iteration 1).\n71: - Probing the built CLI read-only under four switch names (canonical, master, SPECKIT_ alias, MK_ alias) confirmed the envelope and the abstain reason without starting a daemon (iteration 1).\n72: - Reading the CLI JSON manifest after the candidate workspace-root bypass showed `advisor_recommend` does not admit `workspaceRoot` at all, so the bypass has no reach and was ruled out (iteration 1).\n73: - Reading the launcher child-env filter against the pass-five diff confirmed the two switch names were removed from the exact-set allowlist (iteration 1).\n74: - Comparing the resolver's `MASTER_ALIASES` and `LEGACY_ALIASES` against the env index and the hooks README found the alias-column drift in one place instead of two guessed ones (iteration 2).\n75: - Reading CP-003's control command against the full alias set found a scenario defect that a switch-only read would miss; the read-only probe reproduced it under `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` (iteration 2).\n76: - Reading each test fixture against `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` rather than the test name found both boundary gaps: the launcher fixture sets two names and the CLI loop excludes the `MK_` set (iteration 3).\n77: - Listing `runtime/lib/*.ts` against the README tree found five missing modules and a second disagreement with the key-files table (iteration 3).\n78: - Replaying the six active sites instead of opening a new direction confirmed the set is stable and that no P2 was silently downgraded in synthesis (iteration 4).\n79: - Reading the holdout files through `jq del(.prompt)` for counts only kept the hygiene rule while proving the files are present (224/63/36 rows) (iteration 4).\n80: \n81: ---\n82: \n83: ## 7. WHAT FAILED\n84: - Checking `disabledRecommendOutput` alone made the workspace-root bypass look live; the CLI schema and the handler parse boundaries were needed to disprove it (iteration 1).\n85: - Reading the ENV-REFERENCE preamble as a licence to ignore the Source column was too generous: the row's own description claims the direct call, so the direct-call surface still has to be named (iteration 2).\n86: - Trusting the launcher test's name (\"keeps the per-request advisor switch out of the daemon env\") instead of its fixture would have marked the whole switch set covered; the fixture names only two keys (iteration 3).\n87: - No clean route to a graph-backed convergence existed: the coverage graph stayed unavailable, so the run must stop at `maxIterationsReached` rather than claim `converged` (iteration 4).\n88: \n89: ---\n90: \n91: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n92: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n93: ### **`INSTALL-GUIDE.md` rollback table is wrong**: it names `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED` as the switch; the resolver honors it and the CLI abstains under it. Ruled out. -- BLOCKED (iteration 2, 1 attempts)\n94: - What was tried: **`INSTALL-GUIDE.md` rollback table is wrong**: it names `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED` as the switch; the resolver honors it and the CLI abstains under it. Ruled out.\n95: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n96: - Do NOT retry: **`INSTALL-GUIDE.md` rollback table is wrong**: it names `SPECKIT