{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780673445,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","part":{"partID":"prt_1e143b0c3001f03ehHLDwC282f","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","messageID":"msg_1e143a31c001zXA3jCAlVk2QgD","type":"tool","id":"call_4561a1a89ae64c05b99b0b1b","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"D13\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/plan.md | head -20; echo \"=== report-2 limits ===\"; grep -n -i \"limit\\|not a finding\\|reject\\|ruled out\\|accepted\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/scratch/review/report-2.txt | head -30"},"output":"85:**Limit kept.** A shell call that becomes write events hides any document read in the same call, which a redirect already does today: `cat <doc> > notes.md` prints `kinds=write startedCommand=null` (spec Measured Behavior). After this change `cat <doc> | tee notes.md` and `cp <doc> x.md` read the same way, and T003 pins that parity. Keeping a read beside the writes would also move every stored redirect run, so it is recorded in D13 rather than folded in.\n87:**Rejected.** Reading a Python, Node or other interpreter write. Its target is only known by running its code, so the `python write` line stays `kinds=shell`, recorded in D13. Treating every unknown shell call as a write, which would mark every `ls` unsafe.\n123:**Rejected.** Checking the four tracked absolute links under `specs/**/scratch`. They arrive through `git clone`, so `copyPath` never sees them (D13).\n169:### Decision D13: recorded, not built\n219:- Same-class producers: `rg -n \"new URL\\('\\.\\./\\.\\./\\.\\./\\.\\./\\.\\./\\.\\./hooks/shared\" .skilled/skills --glob '*.ts' --glob '!**/dist/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**'` lists the fixed-hop sources. One is built (T022) and the rest are recorded (D13). `rg -n \"'-Rc'|cp -R\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor --glob '!**/node_modules/**'` lists every copy call.\n=== report-2 limits ===\n3:P2 .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1047 (Q2) SHELL_COMMAND_FLAG needs `c` as the last letter, so a cluster with `c` before another letter, which bash accepts, is not read as nested text. BASE caught it through the plain split, with a garbled path. Wrappers outside the shell list (`fish -c`, `ssh host \"...\"`, `watch \"...\"`) lose the same garbled BASE write. That is the same class as the accepted su -c case, so they are noted here and not graded on their own. | evidence: same probe: `bash -cx 'cd x; rm a.md'` BASE [\"a.md'\"] FIX [], `fish -c \"cd x; rm a.md\"` BASE [\"a.md\\\"\"] FIX [], `ssh host \"cd x; rm a.md\"` and `watch \"cd x; rm a.md\"` each BASE [\"a.md\\\"\"] FIX [] | fix: use /^-[A-Za-z]*c[A-Za-z]*$/, and name the wrapper class beside su -c in the accepted risks\n5:P2 .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:287 (Q3) The stale rule now refuses the committed hook edit, which closes the first report's P1. It also widens the over-refusal plan D2 accepted for the dist's own folder to every tracked file under a reached folder. In the real advisor runtime that covers hooks/*.md, hooks/*/README.md, hooks/tests, the .mjs adapters and hooks/pi, which tsconfig.build.json excludes. So a current build is refused after a doc-only commit there, and this commit's own hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md edit is such a case. Plan D2 still states only the own-folder rule. No under-refusal was found: of the six ignored dist trees, only the advisor's tsconfig include climbs out of its folder, and the advisor's imports outside runtime/ and hooks/ come through @spec-kit/shared, which has its own checked dist. | evidence: probe under mktemp in TMPDIR with the real runtime/tsconfig.build.json copied in. Clean and current: `{\"ok\":true,...,\"copied\":[\"skill/runtime/dist\"]}` exit=0. Committed hooks/claude/hook.ts edit: `stale_build` exit=2. Only skill/hooks/README.md newer, hook.ts older than the build: `stale_build` exit=2. A tsconfig scan of every ignored dist printed one climbing include, \"../hooks/**/*.ts\" | fix: count only files matching the include patterns minus exclude (or only *.ts under a reached folder), or record the widened cost in plan D2\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"85:**Limit kept.** A shell call that becomes write events hides any document read in the same call, which a redirect already does today: `cat <doc> > notes.md` prints `kinds=write startedCommand=null` (spec Measured Behavior). After this change `cat <doc> | tee notes.md` and `cp <doc> x.md` read the same way, and T003 pins that parity. Keeping a read beside the writes would also move every stored redirect run, so it is recorded in D13 rather than folded in.\n87:**Rejected.** Reading a Python, Node or other interpreter write. Its target is only known by running its code, so the `python write` line stays `kinds=shell`, recorded in D13. Treating every unknown shell call as a write, which would mark every `ls` unsafe.\n123:**Rejected.** Checking the four tracked absolute links under `specs/**/scratch`. They arrive through `git clone`, so `copyPath` never sees them (D13).\n169:### Decision D13: recorded, not built\n219:- Same-class producers: `rg -n \"new URL\\('\\.\\./\\.\\./\\.\\./\\.\\./\\.\\./\\.\\./hooks/shared\" .skilled/skills --glob '*.ts' --glob '!**/dist/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**'` lists the fixed-hop sources. One is built (T022) and the rest are recorded (D13). `rg -n \"'-Rc'|cp -R\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor --glob '!**/node_modules/**'` lists every copy call.\n=== report-2 limits ===\n3:P2 .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1047 (Q2) SHELL_COMMAND_FLAG needs `c` as the last letter, so a cluster with `c` before another letter, which bash accepts, is not read as nested text. BASE caught it through the plain split, with a garbled path. Wrappers outside the shell list (`fish -c`, `ssh host \"...\"`, `watch \"...\"`) lose the same garbled BASE write. That is the same class as the accepted su -c case, so they are noted here and not graded on their own. | evidence: same probe: `bash -cx 'cd x; rm a.md'` BASE [\"a.md'\"] FIX [], `fish -c \"cd x; rm a.md\"` BASE [\"a.md\\\"\"] FIX [], `ssh host \"cd x; rm a.md\"` and `watch \"cd x; rm a.md\"` each BASE [\"a.md\\\"\"] FIX [] | fix: use /^-[A-Za-z]*c[A-Za-z]*$/, and name the wrapper class beside su -c in the accepted risks\n5:P2 .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:287 (Q3) The stale rule now refuses the committed hook edit, which closes the first report's P1. It also widens the over-refusal plan D2 accepted for the dist's own folder to every tracked file under a reached folder. In the real advisor runtime that covers hooks/*.md, hooks/*/README.md, hooks/tests, the .mjs adapters and hooks/pi, which tsconfig.build.json excludes. So a current build is refused after a doc-only commit there, and this commit's own hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md edit is such a case. Plan D2 still states only the own-folder rule. No under-refusal was found: of the six ignored dist trees, only the advisor's tsconfig include climbs out of its folder, and the advisor's imports outside runtime/ and hooks/ come through @spec-kit/shared, which has its own checked dist. | evidence: probe under mktemp in TMPDIR with the real runtime/tsconfig.build.json copied in. Clean and current: `{\"ok\":true,...,\"copied\":[\"skill/runtime/dist\"]}` exit=0. Committed hooks/claude/hook.ts edit: `stale_build` exit=2. Only skill/hooks/README.md newer, hook.ts older than the build: `stale_build` exit=2. A tsconfig scan of every ignored dist printed one climbing include, \"../hooks/**/*.ts\" | fix: count only files matching the include patterns minus exclude (or only *.ts under a reached folder), or record the widened cost in plan D2\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"D13\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/plan.md | head -20; echo \\\"=== report-2 limits ===\\\"; grep -n -i \\\"limit\\\\|not a finding\\\\|reject\\\\|ruled out\\\\|accepted\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/scratch/review/report-2.txt | head -30\"}"},"time":{"start":1794780672195,"end":1794780673445}}}}
