{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780762216,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","part":{"partID":"prt_1e1450a21001wOI2VsPJ4nLieC","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","messageID":"msg_1e144dbd10013fyt4JeUyOJvzz","type":"tool","id":"call_bdf742e326b34bfa9f0a73f2","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '40,150p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md"},"output":"       └───────────▶  │ Freshness     │ ───▶   │ Compatibility  │\n                      │ daemon        │        │ lifecycle      │\n                      └───────┬───────┘        └────────────────┘\n                              │\n                              ▼\n                      ┌───────────────┐\n                      │ Shadow data   │\n                      └───────────────┘\n\nDependency direction: handlers/scripts -> lib -> schemas and shared helpers\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY\n\n```text\nlib/\n+-- auth/                       # Trusted caller checks\n+-- compat/                     # Compatibility and daemon probes\n+-- cross-skill-edges/          # Inbound enhances edge detection/apply helpers\n+-- daemon/                     # Advisor daemon helpers\n+-- derived/                    # Derived metadata helpers\n+-- embedders/                  # Advisor embedder schema and shared registry shims\n+-- freshness/                  # Freshness and cache state helpers\n+-- ipc/                        # Launcher IPC bridge and idle-timeout helpers\n+-- lifecycle/                  # Skill lifecycle metadata helpers\n+-- scorer/                     # Advisor scorer implementation\n+-- shadow/                     # Shadow-mode telemetry helpers\n+-- shared/                     # Small advisor-local shared helpers\n+-- utils/                      # Small utility functions\n+-- advisor-runtime-values.ts   # Runtime defaults and constants\n+-- policy-plan.ts              # Advisor policy delivery-state machine + observed-receipt confirmation (epoch>=1 floor)\n+-- prompt-policy.ts            # Prompt handling policy\n+-- render.ts                   # Prompt-safe output rendering\n+-- subprocess.ts               # Child-process wrapper helpers\n`-- README.md\n```\n\nAllowed direction:\n\n```text\nhandlers -> lib modules\nscripts -> lib modules\nlib modules -> schemas and shared utilities\n```\n\nDisallowed direction:\n\n```text\nlib modules -> tool registration\nlib modules -> test fixtures\nsubfolders -> handlers for runtime behavior\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n\n```text\nlib/\n+-- advisor-disabled.ts\n+-- advisor-runtime-values.ts\n+-- affordance-normalizer.ts\n+-- caller-context.ts\n+-- command-attach.ts\n+-- compiled-routing-flag.ts\n+-- df-idf.ts\n+-- error-diagnostics.ts\n+-- freshness.ts\n+-- generation.ts\n+-- metrics.ts\n+-- normalize-adapter-output.ts\n+-- policy-plan.ts\n+-- private-skill-target.cjs\n+-- private-skill-target.ts\n+-- prompt-cache.ts\n+-- prompt-policy.ts\n+-- render.ts\n+-- route-exclusions.ts\n+-- skill-advisor-brief.ts\n+-- source-cache.ts\n+-- subprocess.ts\n+-- auth/\n+-- compat/\n+-- cross-skill-edges/\n+-- daemon/\n+-- derived/\n+-- embedders/\n+-- freshness/\n+-- ipc/\n+-- lifecycle/\n+-- scorer/\n+-- shadow/\n+-- shared/\n+-- skill-graph/\n+-- utils/\n`-- README.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. KEY FILES\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `advisor-runtime-values.ts` | Runtime constants and defaults used by advisor paths. |\n| `affordance-normalizer.ts` | Normalizes prompt affordance signals before scoring. |\n| `command-attach.ts` | `attachCommand()` names the slash command for a hub recommendation whose compiled route picks one `workflowMode`. It reads the `MODE_COMMANDS` table that `derive-command-bridges.cjs` generates from each hub's `mode-registry.json`. A `system-deep-loop` command needs the same command typed in the prompt or a `DEPTH_WORDING` phrase, and a prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command. `commandOnlyMentioned()` reads how the prompt names a command, and a command the prompt refuses or asks about is not offered unless a later clause asks for it. A correction inside an existing document carries no `/create:readme`, `/create:feature-catalog` or `/create:manual-testing-playbook`. The module has no imports. |\n| `prompt-policy.ts` | Applies prompt-safe routing and rendering policy. |\n| `render.ts` | Renders advisor results into prompt-safe output. |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"       └───────────▶  │ Freshness     │ ───▶   │ Compatibility  │\n                      │ daemon        │        │ lifecycle      │\n                      └───────┬───────┘        └────────────────┘\n                              │\n                              ▼\n                      ┌───────────────┐\n                      │ Shadow data   │\n                      └───────────────┘\n\nDependency direction: handlers/scripts -> lib -> schemas and shared helpers\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY\n\n```text\nlib/\n+-- auth/                       # Trusted caller checks\n+-- compat/                     # Compatibility and daemon probes\n+-- cross-skill-edges/          # Inbound enhances edge detection/apply helpers\n+-- daemon/                     # Advisor daemon helpers\n+-- derived/                    # Derived metadata helpers\n+-- embedders/                  # Advisor embedder schema and shared registry shims\n+-- freshness/                  # Freshness and cache state helpers\n+-- ipc/                        # Launcher IPC bridge and idle-timeout helpers\n+-- lifecycle/                  # Skill lifecycle metadata helpers\n+-- scorer/                     # Advisor scorer implementation\n+-- shadow/                     # Shadow-mode telemetry helpers\n+-- shared/                     # Small advisor-local shared helpers\n+-- utils/                      # Small utility functions\n+-- advisor-runtime-values.ts   # Runtime defaults and constants\n+-- policy-plan.ts              # Advisor policy delivery-state machine + observed-receipt confirmation (epoch>=1 floor)\n+-- prompt-policy.ts            # Prompt handling policy\n+-- render.ts                   # Prompt-safe output rendering\n+-- subprocess.ts               # Child-process wrapper helpers\n`-- README.md\n```\n\nAllowed direction:\n\n```text\nhandlers -> lib modules\nscripts -> lib modules\nlib modules -> schemas and shared utilities\n```\n\nDisallowed direction:\n\n```text\nlib modules -> tool registration\nlib modules -> test fixtures\nsubfolders -> handlers for runtime behavior\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n\n```text\nlib/\n+-- advisor-disabled.ts\n+-- advisor-runtime-values.ts\n+-- affordance-normalizer.ts\n+-- caller-context.ts\n+-- command-attach.ts\n+-- compiled-routing-flag.ts\n+-- df-idf.ts\n+-- error-diagnostics.ts\n+-- freshness.ts\n+-- generation.ts\n+-- metrics.ts\n+-- normalize-adapter-output.ts\n+-- policy-plan.ts\n+-- private-skill-target.cjs\n+-- private-skill-target.ts\n+-- prompt-cache.ts\n+-- prompt-policy.ts\n+-- render.ts\n+-- route-exclusions.ts\n+-- skill-advisor-brief.ts\n+-- source-cache.ts\n+-- subprocess.ts\n+-- auth/\n+-- compat/\n+-- cross-skill-edges/\n+-- daemon/\n+-- derived/\n+-- embedders/\n+-- freshness/\n+-- ipc/\n+-- lifecycle/\n+-- scorer/\n+-- shadow/\n+-- shared/\n+-- skill-graph/\n+-- utils/\n`-- README.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. KEY FILES\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `advisor-runtime-values.ts` | Runtime constants and defaults used by advisor paths. |\n| `affordance-normalizer.ts` | Normalizes prompt affordance signals before scoring. |\n| `command-attach.ts` | `attachCommand()` names the slash command for a hub recommendation whose compiled route picks one `workflowMode`. It reads the `MODE_COMMANDS` table that `derive-command-bridges.cjs` generates from each hub's `mode-registry.json`. A `system-deep-loop` command needs the same command typed in the prompt or a `DEPTH_WORDING` phrase, and a prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command. `commandOnlyMentioned()` reads how the prompt names a command, and a command the prompt refuses or asks about is not offered unless a later clause asks for it. A correction inside an existing document carries no `/create:readme`, `/create:feature-catalog` or `/create:manual-testing-playbook`. The module has no imports. |\n| `prompt-policy.ts` | Applies prompt-safe routing and rendering policy. |\n| `render.ts` | Renders advisor results into prompt-safe output. |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '40,150p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794780760609,"end":1794780762216}}}}
