{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780783156,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","part":{"partID":"prt_1e1455ebc001FUC1WQwTl1vcUf","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","messageID":"msg_1e14515ba00121Tx8BmC3sQshA","type":"tool","id":"call_e35658bd89154acb92d8f307","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '160,200p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/plan.md; echo \"=== report-3 head ===\"; head -6 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/scratch/review/report-3.txt"},"output":"\n**Why.** D1 and D4 change what the scorer reads from a stored session, which the floors and eval never show. Phase 026's arm was stopped by the operator before scoring, so scoring it here would produce the verdict the operator declined.\n\n### Decision D12: one Opus review, then DeepSeek on the fix diff\n\n**Decision.** One Opus reviewer reads `G diff BASE FIX` read-only. Then round `5b` runs four `cli-opencode` lineages on `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` at reasoning effort `max`, three iterations each, one per area, labelled `accuracy-runner-confirm-5b`, `kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b`, `vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b` and `docs-metadata-confirm-5b`, over a scope file that lists only the fix commit's paths. A P1 that reproduces becomes a task, a new fix commit and one closing round `5c` over that commit's diff. No round past `5c` runs. The synthesis moves the pass-four report to `review/review-report-pass-4.md` and writes the pass-five report, counting rows whose `_lineages` end in `-5`, `-5b` or `-5c`.\n\n**Why.** It is the shape of pass four's rounds `4b` and `4c` (`review/review-report.md`, phase 027 T024 to T026), with one lineage per pass-five area.\n\n### Decision D13: recorded, not built\n\n| Item | File and line | Reason |\n|------|---------------|--------|\n| `R1-P2-002` | `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-mistral-vibe/references/guards-and-hooks.md:184`, `:195` | Rejected by the verifier: the field is documented and the code handles it |\n| Interpreter writes | `RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs` `normalize` | A Python or Node write's target is only known by running it. The probe's `python write` line stays `kinds=shell` |\n| A document read in the same shell call as a write | `RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs` `normalize` and `readDocument` (`:979-993`) | A redirect hides it today, and keeping it would move every stored redirect run. D1 keeps parity |\n| Tracked absolute symlinks | four links under `specs/**/scratch`, found with `git ls-files -s` mode `120000` | `git clone` brings them, not `copyPath` |\n| The fixed six-hop resolver path in other sources | `SAD/hooks/claude/directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts:18` and 13 sources under `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/` (`claude`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin`) | No finding grades them, every compiled copy resolves, and the spec-kit sources are another skill's |\n| The registry severity of the remote guard | `review/deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `iter3-P1-remote-guard-first-turn-only` | Merged output, graded P2 by the verifier |\n| Scoring phase 026's arm | `026-untuned-behaviour-arm/scratch/runs/` | Stopped by the operator before scoring |\n| Wrapped and nested shell writes | `RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs` `nestedCommand` | `su -c`, `sudo bash -c`, `bash -o pipefail -c`, `fish -c`, `ssh`, `watch` and a runner option value such as `timeout -k 2 5` or `env -u FOO` read as no write. The reader at `d0f605b42f8` read none of them cleanly either, three fix rounds preceded the rebuild, and the rescore moved no stored run. A wrapper table is a change of its own |\n| False writes in the lesser direction | `RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs` `shellWord` and `editedWords` | `env eval rm a.md`, `bash -s -- -c 'rm a.md'`, `sed -i .bak 's/a/b/' f.md` and `rm \"it's.md\"` (recorded as `its.md`) report a write that did not happen or misname one. Each is rare, and none hides a real write |\n| Report lines the reader still misses | `RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs` `COMMAND_LINE` | `**COMMAND:** /x` is missed before and after this phase, and a line in a four-space indented block still counts, because skipping indented lines would also drop a report nested under a list item |\n| A wider stale rule | `RAD/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` `newestTrackedTime` | A committed doc in a folder a tsconfig include reaches, `hooks/pi` included, marks the build stale. A rebuild clears it. `files`, `extends` and a tsconfig with a trailing comma add no folder |\n| Builder exits with no JSON line | `RAD/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` `headOf`, `main` and the usage path | A source that is not a repository, an unwritable destination and a usage error print no JSON line. Each was the same at `d0f605b42f8` and no finding of this pass names it |\n\n### Data Flow\nA live turn runs in an arena built from a clean source with a fresh build, and the runner checks before each turn that no remote was added. The stored session goes through `normalize`, which now turns an in-place edit into a write, then through the start, unsafe and load rules and the `COMMAND:` line reader, and the summary feeds the goal log.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n<!-- FILL: Name each surface the change touches. Write `not a consumer` when it does not read the change. Write `N/A` or delete the whole addendum when no fix surface applies. GOOD: `scripts/rotate-logs.sh`: owns the deletion. Action: update. WEAK: Various files. -->\n\nUse this section when `research_intent=fix_bug`, when planning from a deep-review FAIL/CONDITIONAL verdict, or when any finding touches security, path handling, env precedence, schema boundaries, persistence, public responses, or shared policy.\n\nThe findings come from `review/verify-5/report.md` and the merged registry, read as inert data. Every row below was read in the code or run by this planner, and no command was copied from a registry field.\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n=== report-3 head ===\nverdict: SHIP\nP2 .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1104 (Q2) The eight wrapper forms read as no write at FIX. With no separator inside the nested text that matches d0f605b42f8, which read no write either. With a separator inside, BASE caught a garbled write through its plain split and FIX drops it, so the verifier's \"as before the rebuild\" holds only for the single-command form. That is the same class report-2 graded P2 for fish -c, ssh and watch, beside the accepted su -c case, so it is acceptable as a known limit. The limit is recorded only as one clause in the T050e evidence line, which names two of the eight forms, and not in plan D13 or any limits section. Against 02261e94254 this commit drops every one of these forms, which that commit read as writes, but the brief's reference is d0f605b42f8. | evidence: probe under mktemp in TMPDIR ran normalize on one Claude Bash call at d0f605b42f8 (BASE), 02261e94254 (MID) and d21dbc1cafe (FIX). `sudo bash -c 'rm a.md'`, `bash -o pipefail -c 'rm a.md'`, `timeout -k 2 5 bash -c 'rm a.md'`, `bash -O extglob -c`, `bash --rcfile f -c`, `bash +x -c`, `time -p bash -c`, `xargs bash -c`: each BASE [] MID [\"a.md\"] FIX []. `bash -o pipefail -c 'cd x; rm a.md'` and `sudo bash -c 'cd x; rm a.md'`: each BASE [\"a.md'\"] MID [\"x/a.md\"] FIX [] | fix: name the wrapper class (sudo, xargs, a shell option that takes a value, a runner option that takes a value) beside su -c in plan D13\nP2 .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1062 (Q2) Part of that limit is in the new runner code, not only in shell grammar. The comment says a runner's own words are read before the shell, but afterRunner skips only words that start with `-`, so the value of a value-taking option becomes the \"command\": `timeout -k 2 5` stops at 5, `timeout -s KILL 5` stops at 5, and `env -u FOO` (:1068) stops at FOO. Each then reads no write. BASE read none for these either, so nothing is lost against d0f605b42f8. | evidence: same probe: `timeout -k 2 5 bash -c 'rm a.md'`, `timeout -s KILL 5 bash -c 'rm a.md'`, `env -u FOO bash -c 'rm a.md'` each BASE [] MID [\"a.md\"] FIX [] | fix: consume the value word after timeout -k and -s and after env -u, with one case in the T050e table\nP2 .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1053 (Q2) A runner word before `eval` adds a false write against d0f605b42f8. `env`, `nohup`, `nice`, `timeout` and `exec` run an external program, and eval is a shell builtin with no file on this system, so the command fails and changes nothing, while FIX reads a write. Only `command` and `time` can run eval. MID read the same writes, so this commit did not add them against MID. Contrived, so P2. | evidence: same probe: `env eval rm a.md`, `nohup eval rm a.md`, `nice eval rm a.md`, `timeout 5 eval rm a.md`, `exec eval rm a.md` each BASE [] FIX [\"a.md\"]. Real shell under the mktemp folder: `ls /usr/bin/eval` printed No such file, `env eval rm a.md` printed `env: eval: No such file or directory` and a.md was still listed | fix: after a runner, accept `eval` only when every runner word was `command` or `time`\nP2 .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1104 (Q2) The option scan after a shell name does not stop at `--`, so a `-c` after it is read as the command flag. After `--` bash takes `-c` and the next word as positional arguments, so the call changes nothing, while FIX reads a write. MID read the same. Contrived, so P2. | evidence: same probe: `bash -s -- -c 'rm a.md'` BASE [] MID [\"a.md\"] FIX [\"a.md\"]. Real shell: `bash -s -- -c 'rm b.md' </dev/null` left b.md listed | fix: break the option scan on `--`, with one no-write case in the T050e table\nQ1: closed. Every case T050e names reads as asked at FIX. `mkdir -p eval reports` BASE [\"eval\",\"reports\"] MID [] FIX [\"eval\",\"reports\"]. `echo eval rm a.md` BASE [] MID [\"a.md\"] FIX []. `grep bash -c 'rm x.md' notes.md` BASE [] MID [\"x.md\"] FIX []. `bash -cx 'rm a.md'` BASE [] MID [] FIX [\"a.md\"], and a real `bash -cx 'rm c.md'` removed c.md. The rest of the report-2 table also reads right: `rm -rf eval out.json` FIX [\"eval\",\"out.json\"], `touch eval notes.md` FIX [\"eval\",\"notes.md\"], `printf %s eval touch done.md` FIX [], `bash script.sh -c 'rm a.md'` FIX [], `bash -cx 'cd x; rm a.md'` FIX [\"x/a.md\"] (BASE [\"a.md'\"]). The T050c nested cases keep their result: `bash -c 'rm a.md'`, `eval rm a.md`, `timeout 5 bash -lc 'rm a.md'`, `env FOO=1 bash -c`, `nohup sh -c`, `nice -n 5 bash -c` each FIX [\"a.md\"]. | evidence: probe tables c1 and c2 (61 commands) under mktemp in TMPDIR, `git diff 02261e94254 d21dbc1cafe -- .skilled <three excludes>` read, `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` printed `Test Files 1 passed (1)` `Tests 330 passed (330)`, exit 0\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n**Why.** D1 and D4 change what the scorer reads from a stored session, which the floors and eval never show. Phase 026's arm was stopped by the operator before scoring, so scoring it here would produce the verdict the operator declined.\n\n### Decision D12: one Opus review, then DeepSeek on the fix diff\n\n**Decision.** One Opus reviewer reads `G diff BASE FIX` read-only. Then round `5b` runs four `cli-opencode` lineages on `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` at reasoning effort `max`, three iterations each, one per area, labelled `accuracy-runner-confirm-5b`, `kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b`, `vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b` and `docs-metadata-confirm-5b`, over a scope file that lists only the fix commit's paths. A P1 that reproduces becomes a task, a new fix commit and one closing round `5c` over that commit's diff. No round past `5c` runs. The synthesis moves the pass-four report to `review/review-report-pass-4.md` and writes the pass-five report, counting rows whose `_lineages` end in `-5`, `-5b` or `-5c`.\n\n**Why.** It is the shape of pass four's rounds `4b` and `4c` (`review/review-report.md`, phase 027 T024 to T026), with one lineage per pass-five area.\n\n### Decision D13: recorded, not built\n\n| Item | File and line | Reason |\n|------|---------------|--------|\n| `R1-P2-002` | `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-mistral-vibe/references/guards-and-hooks.md:184`, `:195` | Rejected by the verifier: the field is documented and the code handles it |\n| Interpreter writes | `RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs` `normalize` | A Python or Node write's target is only known by running it. The probe's `python write` line stays `kinds=shell` |\n| A document read in the same shell call as a write | `RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs` `normalize` and `readDocument` (`:979-993`) | A redirect hides it today, and keeping it would move every stored redirect run. D1 keeps parity |\n| Tracked absolute symlinks | four links under `specs/**/scratch`, found with `git ls-files -s` mode `120000` | `git clone` brings them, not `copyPath` |\n| The fixed six-hop resolver path in other sources | `SAD/hooks/claude/directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts:18` and 13 sources under `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/` (`claude`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin`) | No finding grades them, every compiled copy resolves, and the spec-kit sources are another skill's |\n| The registry severity of the remote guard | `review/deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `iter3-P1-remote-guard-first-turn-only` | Merged output, graded P2 by the verifier |\n| Scoring phase 026's arm | `026-untuned-behaviour-arm/scratch/runs/` | Stopped by the operator before scoring |\n| Wrapped and nested shell writes | `RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs` `nestedCommand` | `su -c`, `sudo bash -c`, `bash -o pipefail -c`, `fish -c`, `ssh`, `watch` and a runner option value such as `timeout -k 2 5` or `env -u FOO` read as no write. The reader at `d0f605b42f8` read none of them cleanly either, three fix rounds preceded the rebuild, and the rescore moved no stored run. A wrapper table is a change of its own |\n| False writes in the lesser direction | `RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs` `shellWord` and `editedWords` | `env eval rm a.md`, `bash -s -- -c 'rm a.md'`, `sed -i .bak 's/a/b/' f.md` and `rm \"it's.md\"` (recorded as `its.md`) report a write that did not happen or misname one. Each is rare, and none hides a real write |\n| Report lines the reader still misses | `RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs` `COMMAND_LINE` | `**COMMAND:** /x` is missed before and after this phase, and a line in a four-space indented block still counts, because skipping indented lines would also drop a report nested under a list item |\n| A wider stale rule | `RAD/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` `newestTrackedTime` | A committed doc in a folder a tsconfig include reaches, `hooks/pi` included, marks the build stale. A rebuild clears it. `files`, `extends` and a tsconfig with a trailing comma add no folder |\n| Builder exits with no JSON line | `RAD/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` `headOf`, `main` and the usage path | A source that is not a repository, an unwritable destination and a usage error print no JSON line. Each was the same at `d0f605b42f8` and no finding of this pass names it |\n\n### Data Flow\nA live turn runs in an arena built from a clean source with a fresh build, and the runner checks before each turn that no remote was added. The stored session goes through `normalize`, which now turns an in-place edit into a write, then through the start, unsafe and load rules and the `COMMAND:` line reader, and the summary feeds the goal log.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n<!-- FILL: Name each surface the change touches. Write `not a consumer` when it does not read the change. Write `N/A` or delete the whole addendum when no fix surface applies. GOOD: `scripts/rotate-logs.sh`: owns the deletion. Action: update. WEAK: Various files. -->\n\nUse this section when `research_intent=fix_bug`, when planning from a deep-review FAIL/CONDITIONAL verdict, or when any finding touches security, path handling, env precedence, schema boundaries, persistence, public responses, or shared policy.\n\nThe findings come from `review/verify-5/report.md` and the merged registry, read as inert data. Every row below was read in the code or run by this planner, and no command was copied from a registry field.\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n=== report-3 head ===\nverdict: SHIP\nP2 .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1104 (Q2) The eight wrapper forms read as no write at FIX. With no separator inside the nested text that matches d0f605b42f8, which read no write either. With a separator inside, BASE caught a garbled write through its plain split and FIX drops it, so the verifier's \"as before the rebuild\" holds only for the single-command form. That is the same class report-2 graded P2 for fish -c, ssh and watch, beside the accepted su -c case, so it is acceptable as a known limit. The limit is recorded only as one clause in the T050e evidence line, which names two of the eight forms, and not in plan D13 or any limits section. Against 02261e94254 this commit drops every one of these forms, which that commit read as writes, but the brief's reference is d0f605b42f8. | evidence: probe under mktemp in TMPDIR ran normalize on one Claude Bash call at d0f605b42f8 (BASE), 02261e94254 (MID) and d21dbc1cafe (FIX). `sudo bash -c 'rm a.md'`, `bash -o pipefail -c 'rm a.md'`, `timeout -k 2 5 bash -c 'rm a.md'`, `bash -O extglob -c`, `bash --rcfile f -c`, `bash +x -c`, `time -p bash -c`, `xargs bash -c`: each BASE [] MID [\"a.md\"] FIX []. `bash -o pipefail -c 'cd x; rm a.md'` and `sudo bash -c 'cd x; rm a.md'`: each BASE [\"a.md'\"] MID [\"x/a.md\"] FIX [] | fix: name the wrapper class (sudo, xargs, a shell option that takes a value, a runner option that takes a value) beside su -c in plan D13\nP2 .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1062 (Q2) Part of that limit is in the new runner code, not only in shell grammar. The comment says a runner's own words are read before the shell, but afterRunner skips only words that start with `-`, so the value of a value-taking option becomes the \"command\": `timeout -k 2 5` stops at 5, `timeout -s KILL 5` stops at 5, and `env -u FOO` (:1068) stops at FOO. Each then reads no write. BASE read none for these either, so nothing is lost against d0f605b42f8. | evidence: same probe: `timeout -k 2 5 bash -c 'rm a.md'`, `timeout -s KILL 5 bash -c 'rm a.md'`, `env -u FOO bash -c 'rm a.md'` each BASE [] MID [\"a.md\"] FIX [] | fix: consume the value word after timeout -k and -s and after env -u, with one case in the T050e table\nP2 .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1053 (Q2) A runner word before `eval` adds a false write against d0f605b42f8. `env`, `nohup`, `nice`, `timeout` and `exec` run an external program, and eval is a shell builtin with no file on this system, so the command fails and changes nothing, while FIX reads a write. Only `command` and `time` can run eval. MID read the same writes, so this commit did not add them against MID. Contrived, so P2. | evidence: same probe: `env eval rm a.md`, `nohup eval rm a.md`, `nice eval rm a.md`, `timeout 5 eval rm a.md`, `exec eval rm a.md` each BASE [] FIX [\"a.md\"]. Real shell under the mktemp folder: `ls /usr/bin/eval` printed No such file, `env eval rm a.md` printed `env: eval: No such file or directory` and a.md was still listed | fix: after a runner, accept `eval` only when every runner word was `command` or `time`\nP2 .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1104 (Q2) The option scan after a shell name does not stop at `--`, so a `-c` after it is read as the command flag. After `--` bash takes `-c` and the next word as positional arguments, so the call changes nothing, while FIX reads a write. MID read the same. Contrived, so P2. | evidence: same probe: `bash -s -- -c 'rm a.md'` BASE [] MID [\"a.md\"] FIX [\"a.md\"]. Real shell: `bash -s -- -c 'rm b.md' </dev/null` left b.md listed | fix: break the option scan on `--`, with one no-write case in the T050e table\nQ1: closed. Every case T050e names reads as asked at FIX. `mkdir -p eval reports` BASE [\"eval\",\"reports\"] MID [] FIX [\"eval\",\"reports\"]. `echo eval rm a.md` BASE [] MID [\"a.md\"] FIX []. `grep bash -c 'rm x.md' notes.md` BASE [] MID [\"x.md\"] FIX []. `bash -cx 'rm a.md'` BASE [] MID [] FIX [\"a.md\"], and a real `bash -cx 'rm c.md'` removed c.md. The rest of the report-2 table also reads right: `rm -rf eval out.json` FIX [\"eval\",\"out.json\"], `touch eval notes.md` FIX [\"eval\",\"notes.md\"], `printf %s eval touch done.md` FIX [], `bash script.sh -c 'rm a.md'` FIX [], `bash -cx 'cd x; rm a.md'` FIX [\"x/a.md\"] (BASE [\"a.md'\"]). The T050c nested cases keep their result: `bash -c 'rm a.md'`, `eval rm a.md`, `timeout 5 bash -lc 'rm a.md'`, `env FOO=1 bash -c`, `nohup sh -c`, `nice -n 5 bash -c` each FIX [\"a.md\"]. | evidence: probe tables c1 and c2 (61 commands) under mktemp in TMPDIR, `git diff 02261e94254 d21dbc1cafe -- .skilled <three excludes>` read, `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` printed `Test Files 1 passed (1)` `Tests 33