{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780799201,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","part":{"partID":"prt_1e1459d46001lwLAd0vAnCyZ40","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","messageID":"msg_1e1456674001JtaXkkFJ0IKM8p","type":"tool","id":"call_1e69793dea4c468a8d51330c","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && echo \"=== hooks README skill-advisor rows ===\"; rg -n \"SKILL_ADVISOR\" .skilled/hooks/README.md | head -20; echo \"=== INSTALL-GUIDE ===\"; rg -n \"SKILL_ADVISOR_(HOOK_)?DISABLED|SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED\" INSTALL-GUIDE.md 2>/dev/null | head -20"},"output":"=== hooks README skill-advisor rows ===\n44:| `skill-advisor` | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED` | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` | enabled | inject | wired |\n80:- **Environment**: set any flag inline (`SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1 <command>`), for a session (`export SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED=1`), or in your shell profile.\n81:- **Config file**: copy `hook-flags.env.example` to `hook-flags.env` (in this directory) and uncomment the flags you want off. It uses the same `KEY=value` names, is gitignored (personal to you), and is read by every guard variant. A comment can follow a value after a space or tab, so the example's lines work as soon as you uncomment them. Re-enable a file-disabled hook for one session with e.g. `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=0`. `/doctor:env` shows where each switch is set and writes one here after your yes, and the root `.env.example` lists every other setting with its default.\n=== INSTALL-GUIDE ===\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== hooks README skill-advisor rows ===\n44:| `skill-advisor` | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED` | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` | enabled | inject | wired |\n80:- **Environment**: set any flag inline (`SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1 <command>`), for a session (`export SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED=1`), or in your shell profile.\n81:- **Config file**: copy `hook-flags.env.example` to `hook-flags.env` (in this directory) and uncomment the flags you want off. It uses the same `KEY=value` names, is gitignored (personal to you), and is read by every guard variant. A comment can follow a value after a space or tab, so the example's lines work as soon as you uncomment them. Re-enable a file-disabled hook for one session with e.g. `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=0`. `/doctor:env` shows where each switch is set and writes one here after your yes, and the root `.env.example` lists every other setting with its default.\n=== INSTALL-GUIDE ===\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && echo \\\"=== hooks README skill-advisor rows ===\\\"; rg -n \\\"SKILL_ADVISOR\\\" .skilled/hooks/README.md | head -20; echo \\\"=== INSTALL-GUIDE ===\\\"; rg -n \\\"SKILL_ADVISOR_(HOOK_)?DISABLED|SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED\\\" INSTALL-GUIDE.md 2>/dev/null | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794780798278,"end":1794780799201}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780799310,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","part":{"partID":"prt_1e1459805002EyCRFMKfevzsD7","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","messageID":"msg_1e1456674001JtaXkkFJ0IKM8p","type":"tool","id":"call_e6c06b3a923543f99cfdeb1b","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && echo \"=== calls of advisorDisabledBy ===\"; rg -n \"advisorDisabledBy\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime --glob '!**/dist/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' | head -20; echo \"=== other master alias names ===\"; rg -n \"SPECKIT_HOOKS_DISABLED|MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\" .skilled --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**' -l | head -20"},"output":"=== calls of advisorDisabledBy ===\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/advisor-disabled.vitest.ts:15:import { ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS, advisorDisabledBy, disabledRecommendOutput } from '../lib/advisor-disabled.js';\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/advisor-disabled.vitest.ts:18:describe('advisorDisabledBy', () => {\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/advisor-disabled.vitest.ts:20:    expect(advisorDisabledBy({}, {})).toBeNull();\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/advisor-disabled.vitest.ts:27:    expect(advisorDisabledBy({ [flag]: '1' }, {})).toBe(flag);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/advisor-disabled.vitest.ts:31:    expect(advisorDisabledBy({\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/advisor-disabled.vitest.ts:41:    expect(advisorDisabledBy(env, {})).toBeNull();\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/advisor-disabled.vitest.ts:50:    expect(advisorDisabledBy(env, {})).toBe(flag);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/advisor-disabled.vitest.ts:63:describe('advisorDisabledBy with a flags file', () => {\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/advisor-disabled.vit