==\n.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.0.0.md\n.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.0.14.md\n.skilled/bin/tests/worktree-guard.test.sh\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/git-setup-check.test.cjs\n.skilled/hooks/decision-capture/vibe/ask-capture-post-tool.test.mjs\n.skilled/hooks/decision-capture/lib/capture-core.test.mjs\n.skilled/hooks/decision-capture/claude/ask-capture-posttooluse.test.mjs\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.test.cjs\n.skilled/hooks/shared/README.md\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.sh\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md\n.skilled/hooks/dispatch/codex/codex-shell-tool.test.mjs\n.skilled/hooks/dispatch/devin/devin-dispatch-audit.test.mjs\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts\n.skilled/hooks/post-edit-quality/tests/codex-post-edit-quality.test.cjs\n.skilled/hooks/post-edit-quality/tests/devin-post-edit-quality.test.cjs\n.skilled/hooks/session-handover/tests/session-handover-cli.test.cjs\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && echo \\\"=== calls of advisorDisabledBy ===\\\"; rg -n \\\"advisorDisabledBy\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime --glob '!**/dist/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' | head -20; echo \\\"=== other master alias names ===\\\"; rg -n \\\"SPECKIT_HOOKS_DISABLED|MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\\\" .skilled --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**' -l | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794780796933,"end":1794780799310}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794780800366,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","part":{"id":"prt_1e145a56e001Trww5WbZenioch","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","messageID":"msg_1e1456674001JtaXkkFJ0IKM8p","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"38c25f7f78a7a2467e48fa8f32174fc1b132e2bf","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":5297,"output":320,"reasoning":978,"cache":{"read":93824,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794780803160,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","part":{"id":"prt_1e145b058001TYs2cQqeEXmreT","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","messageID":"msg_1e145a573001r6i1TlR48lhgdH","type":"step-start","snapshot":"38c25f7f78a7a2467e48fa8f32174fc1b132e2bf"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780822470,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","part":{"partID":"prt_1e145f38f001SFu0gYy78pnbqy","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","messageID":"msg_1e145a573001r6i1TlR48lhgdH","type":"tool","id":"call_6d1747939e364a41b0aa4eb7","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '30,50p' .skilled/hooks/README.md; echo \"=== env example header ===\"; sed -n '1,20p' .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example; echo \"=== skill-advisor rows in env example ===\"; grep -n \"SKILL_ADVISOR\" .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example"},"output":"A session-handover concern, documented in [session-handover/](./session-handover/README.md), adds context nudges and runtime-specific arming for Claude, Pi, OpenCode and Codex sessions started through skilled-loop. Cursor, Devin and DSH join the same loop on the `/speckit:handoff` command trigger only. Inside skilled-loop the nudge asks for a hop, and outside it only for a note the session keeps through compaction. The sourced `.skilled/bin/skilled-loop-shell.sh` shim starts every plain interactive runtime launch under a trusted wrapper, a symlinked `.skilled` included. Trusted means inside the sourced checkout, a linked worktree registered to it or a checkout in `SKILLED_LOOP_TRUSTED_CHECKOUTS`. Each hop adds a line to a gitignored hop history, and `SESSION_HANDOVER_NOTIFY_HOPS` adds an opt-in macOS notice per hand-over. The concern ships on for Claude Code and off elsewhere: set `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED=1` to turn it on for every runtime, or `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_<RUNTIME>_ENABLED` to turn it on (`1`) or off (`0`) for one.\n\n### Full index\n\nBeyond those real-code cores, this tree is now the **full browsable index of every repo-authored hook**. Skill-owned hooks whose logic is genuinely their skill's engine still keep their **code** in the owning skill, but each is **symlinked in** here under `<concern>/<runtime>/` (the symlink is the index entry, the code stays local): so one directory shows every hook the repo installs, organized by concern and runtime.\n\nEvery concern except `git-message-gate` honors the master `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED` switch and its canonical `SYSTEM_<CONCERN>_DISABLED` switch. The message gate has none on purpose: the commit, PR and branch rules carry no bypass on any surface, and the place to change them is the rules block in the sk-git templates. The default is enabled, except `session-handover`, which ships on for Claude Code and off for every other runtime. The flag that decides is `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_<RUNTIME>_ENABLED` when it holds a value, where `<RUNTIME>` is `CLAUDE`, `CODEX`, `PI`, `OPENCODE`, `CURSOR`, `DEVIN` or `VIBE`, then `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED` when it holds one. With both empty or unset, only Claude Code runs it. So `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED=1` with `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_CLAUDE_ENABLED=0` is on for every runtime except Claude Code. The disable switch and the master switch still win over every enable flag. Truthy disable values are `1`, `true`, `yes`, and `on` (case-insensitive). See the kill-switch index below for the complete concern and alias inventory.\n\n### Kill-switch index\n\nThis table is the single source of truth for repo-authored hook kill-switch names. All concerns are wired to the shared resolver or its shell equivalent.\n\n| Concern | Canonical flag (`SYSTEM_<CONCERN>_DISABLED`) | Legacy aliases | Default | Effect | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `skill-advisor` | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED` | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` | enabled | inject | wired |\n| `spec-gate` | `SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED` | `SPECKIT_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED` | enabled | notice / deny | wired |\n| `completion` | `SYSTEM_COMPLETION_DISABLED` | `SYSTEM_COMPLETION_SENTINEL_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SPECKIT_COMPLETION_DISABLED` | enabled | warn | wired |\n| `decision-capture` | `SYSTEM_DECISION_CAPTURE_DISABLED` | none | enabled | queue (local, for the next save) | wired |\n| `ask-surface` | `SYSTEM_ASK_SURFACE_DISABLED` | none | enabled | re-prompt (Claude, DSH, OpenCode, Pi) / warn (Codex, Devin) | wired |\n| `codex-watchdog` | `CODEX_HOOKS_WATCHDOG_DISABLED` | `CODEX_WATCHDOG_DISABLED` | enabled | warn | wired |\n| `permission-policy` | `SYSTEM_PERMISSION_POLICY_DISABLED` | none | enabled | deny | wired |\n=== env example header ===\n# Hook switch config: copy to hook-flags.env and uncomment what you want to change.\n#\n#   cp .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env\n#\n# Every hook is ON by default except session handover, which ships OFF on every runtime\n# but Claude Code (see its block below). Setting a flag to a truthy value (1 / true / yes / on, case-insensitive)\n# disables that hook. hook-flags.env is gitignored, so your\n# choices stay local. A real environment variable overrides the file, so you can\n# re-enable a file-disabled hook for one session with e.g. SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=0.\n# A comment may follow a value after a space or tab, as on the lines below.\n#\n# Read by .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.{cjs,mjs,ts,sh}. The canonical index of\n# every concern and flag lives in .skilled/hooks/README.md. Every other setting, with\n# its default, is in the root .env.example; set those with an export in your shell\n# profile. /doctor:env shows where each one is set and saves a change after your yes.\n\n# ── Master switch — disables ALL repo-authored hooks at once ──\n# SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED=1\n\n# ── Per-concern switches (alphabetical) ──\n=== skill-advisor rows in env example ===\n9:# re-enable a file-disabled hook for one session with e.g. SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=0.\n47:# SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1         # skill-advisor brief on your prompts and the Gate 2 advisor_recommend direct call\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A session-handover concern, documented in [session-handover/](./session-handover/README.md), adds context nudges and runtime-specific arming for Claude, Pi, OpenCode and Codex sessions started through skilled-loop. Cursor, Devin and DSH join the same loop on the `/speckit:handoff` command trigger only. Inside skilled-loop the nudge asks for a hop, and outside it only for a note the session keeps through compaction. The sourced `.skilled/bin/skilled-loop-shell.sh` shim starts every plain interactive runtime launch under a trusted wrapper, a symlinked `.skilled` included. Trusted means inside the sourced checkout, a linked worktree registered to it or a checkout in `SKILLED_LOOP_TRUSTED_CHECKOUTS`. Each hop adds a line to a gitignored hop history, and `SESSION_HANDOVER_NOTIFY_HOPS` adds an opt-in macOS notice per hand-over. The concern ships on for Claude Code and off elsewhere: set `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED=1` to turn it on for every runtime, or `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_<RUNTIME>_ENABLED` to turn it on (`1`) or off (`0`) for one.\n\n### Full index\n\nBeyond those real-code cores, this tree is now the **full browsable index of every repo-authored hook**. Skill-owned hooks whose logic is genuinely their skill's engine still keep their **code** in the owning skill, but each is **symlinked in** here under `<concern>/<runtime>/` (the symlink is the index entry, the code stays local): so one directory shows every hook the repo installs, organized by concern and runtime.\n\nEvery concern except `git-message-gate` honors the master `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED` switch and its canonical `SYSTEM_<CONCERN>_DISABLED` switch. The message gate has none on purpose: the commit, PR and branch rules carry no bypass on any surface, and the place to change them is the rules block in the sk-git templates. The default is enabled, except `session-handover`, which ships on for Claude Code and off for every other runtime. The flag that decides is `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_<RUNTIME>_ENABLED` when it holds a value, where `<RUNTIME>` is `CLAUDE`, `CODEX`, `PI`, `OPENCODE`, `CURSOR`, `DEVIN` or `VIBE`, then `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED` when it holds one. With both empty or unset, only Claude Code runs it. So `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED=1` with `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_CLAUDE_ENABLED=0` is on for every runtime except Claude Code. The disable switch and the master switch still win over every enable flag. Truthy disable values are `1`, `true`, `yes`, and `on` (case-insensitive). See the kill-switch index below for the complete concern and alias inventory.\n\n### Kill-switch index\n\nThis table is the single source of truth for repo-authored hook kill-switch names. All concerns are wired to the shared resolver or its shell equivalent.\n\n| Concern | Canonical flag (`SYSTEM_<CONCERN>_DISABLED`) | Legacy aliases | Default | Effect | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `skill-advisor` | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED` | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` | enabled | inject | wired |\n| `spec-gate` | `SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED` | `SPECKIT_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED` | enabled | notice / deny | wired |\n| `completion` | `SYSTEM_COMPLETION_DISABLED` | `SYSTEM_COMPLETION_SENTINEL_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SPECKIT_COMPLETION_DISABLED` | enabled | warn | wired |\n| `decision-capture` | `SYSTEM_DECISION_CAPTURE_DISABLED` | none | enabled | queue (local, for the next save) | wired |\n| `ask-surface` | `SYSTEM_ASK_SURFACE_DISABLED` | none | enabled | re-prompt (Claude, DSH, OpenCode, Pi) / warn (Codex, Devin) | wired |\n| `codex-watchdog` | `CODEX_HOOKS_WATCHDOG_DISABLED` | `CODEX_WATCHDOG_DISABLED` | enabled | warn | wired |\n| `permission-policy` | `SYSTEM_PERMISSION_POLICY_DISABLED` | none | enabled | deny | wired |\n=== env example header ===\n# Hook switch config: copy to hook-flags.env and uncomment what you want to change.\n#\n#   cp .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env\n#\n# Every hook is ON by default except session handover, which ships OFF on every runtime\n# but Claude Code (see its block below). Setting a flag to a truthy value (1 / true / yes / on, case-insensitive)\n# disables that hook. hook-flags.env is gitignored, so your\n# choices stay local. A real environment variable overrides the file, so you can\n# re-enable a file-disabled hook for one session with e.g. SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=0.\n# A comment may follow a value after a space or tab, as on the lines below.\n#\n# Read by .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.{cjs,mjs,ts,sh}. The canonical index of\n# every concern and flag lives in .skilled/hooks/README.md. Every other setting, with\n# its default, is in the root .env.example; set those with an export in your shell\n# profile. /doctor:env shows where each one is set and saves a change after your yes.\n\n# ── Master switch — disables ALL repo-authored hooks at once ──\n# SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED=1\n\n# ── Per-concern switches (alphabetical) ──\n=== skill-advisor rows in env example ===\n9:# re-enable a file-disabled hook for one session with e.g. SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=0.\n47:# SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1         # skill-advisor brief on your prompts and the Gate 2 advisor_recommend direct call\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '30,50p' .skilled/hooks/README.md; echo \\\"=== env example header ===\\\"; sed -n '1,20p' .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example; echo \\\"=== skill-advisor rows in env example ===\\\"; grep -n \\\"SKILL_ADVISOR\\\" .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example\"}"},"time":{"start":1794780820367,"end":1794780822470}}}}
