{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780850208,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","part":{"partID":"prt_1e1466242001I5tYHkKKwqtv60","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","messageID":"msg_1e14600ba001gYGYLUqfWmV03T","type":"tool","id":"call_77e70cd90d7e4631b514e6c0","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '230,290p' .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs"},"output":"// kill switch or a legacy alias), \"runtime\" (the runtime's enable switch, which held a\n// value), \"global\" (the global enable switch, unset or set) or \"default\" (a default-on\n// concern, or a default-off one on a runtime DEFAULT_ON_RUNTIMES names). Arguments are\n// those of isHookEnabled.\nfunction hookFlagDecision(concern, env, config, options) {\n  const hasEnv = env !== undefined && env !== null;\n  const source = hasEnv ? env : process.env;\n  const cfg =\n    config !== undefined && config !== null\n      ? config\n      : hasEnv\n        ? EMPTY_CONFIG\n        : fileConfig();\n  const resolve = (key) => {\n    const fromEnv = source[key];\n    return fromEnv !== undefined ? fromEnv : cfg[key];\n  };\n  const holds = (value) => typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() !== \"\";\n  // A switch's own value when it holds one, else its second spelling's when that holds\n  // one, so `key` names whichever switch the operator actually set.\n  const resolveSwitch = (key) => {\n    const value = resolve(key);\n    const alias = holds(value) ? null : switchAlias(key);\n    if (alias && holds(resolve(alias))) return { key: alias, value: resolve(alias) };\n    return { key, value };\n  };\n  for (const key of [MASTER_FLAG].concat(MASTER_ALIASES)) {\n    if (isTruthy(resolve(key))) return { enabled: false, key, reason: \"master\" };\n  }\n  const flag = concernFlag(concern);\n  if (flag) {\n    const kill = resolveSwitch(flag);\n    if (isTruthy(kill.value)) return { enabled: false, key: kill.key, reason: \"kill\" };\n  }\n  for (const key of LEGACY_ALIASES[concern] || []) {\n    if (isTruthy(resolve(key))) return { enabled: false, key, reason: \"kill\" };\n  }\n  if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(DEFAULT_OFF, concern)) {\n    const runtimeFlag = runtimeEnableFlag(concern, options && options.runtime);\n    if (runtimeFlag) {\n      const runtimeSwitch = resolveSwitch(runtimeFlag);\n      if (holds(runtimeSwitch.value)) {\n        return { enabled: isTruthy(runtimeSwitch.value), key: runtimeSwitch.key, reason: \"runtime\" };\n      }\n    }\n    const globalSwitch = resolveSwitch(DEFAULT_OFF[concern]);\n    if (!holds(globalSwitch.value)) {\n      const runtime = options && typeof options.runtime === \"string\" ? options.runtime.trim().toLowerCase() : \"\";\n      if ((DEFAULT_ON_RUNTIMES[concern] || []).includes(runtime)) {\n        return { enabled: true, key: null, reason: \"default\" };\n      }\n    }\n    return { enabled: isTruthy(globalSwitch.value), key: globalSwitch.key, reason: \"global\" };\n  }\n  return { enabled: true, key: null, reason: \"default\" };\n}\n\n// The per-runtime enable switch for a default-off concern, such as\n// SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_CLAUDE_ENABLED, or null when the concern has no enable\n// switch or the runtime is not one of RUNTIMES.\nfunction runtimeEnableFlag(concern, runtime) {\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"// kill switch or a legacy alias), \"runtime\" (the runtime's enable switch, which held a\n// value), \"global\" (the global enable switch, unset or set) or \"default\" (a default-on\n// concern, or a default-off one on a runtime DEFAULT_ON_RUNTIMES names). Arguments are\n// those of isHookEnabled.\nfunction hookFlagDecision(concern, env, config, options) {\n  const hasEnv = env !== undefined && env !== null;\n  const source = hasEnv ? env : process.env;\n  const cfg =\n    config !== undefined && config !== null\n      ? config\n      : hasEnv\n        ? EMPTY_CONFIG\n        : fileConfig();\n  const resolve = (key) => {\n    const fromEnv = source[key];\n    return fromEnv !== undefined ? fromEnv : cfg[key];\n  };\n  const holds = (value) => typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() !== \"\";\n  // A switch's own value when it holds one, else its second spelling's when that holds\n  // one, so `key` names whichever switch the operator actually set.\n  const resolveSwitch = (key) => {\n    const value = resolve(key);\n    const alias = holds(value) ? null : switchAlias(key);\n    if (alias && holds(resolve(alias))) return { key: alias, value: resolve(alias) };\n    return { key, value };\n  };\n  for (const key of [MASTER_FLAG].concat(MASTER_ALIASES)) {\n    if (isTruthy(resolve(key))) return { enabled: false, key, reason: \"master\" };\n  }\n  const flag = concernFlag(concern);\n  if (flag) {\n    const kill = resolveSwitch(flag);\n    if (isTruthy(kill.value)) return { enabled: false, key: kill.key, reason: \"kill\" };\n  }\n  for (const key of LEGACY_ALIASES[concern] || []) {\n    if (isTruthy(resolve(key))) return { enabled: false, key, reason: \"kill\" };\n  }\n  if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(DEFAULT_OFF, concern)) {\n    const runtimeFlag = runtimeEnableFlag(concern, options && options.runtime);\n    if (runtimeFlag) {\n      const runtimeSwitch = resolveSwitch(runtimeFlag);\n      if (holds(runtimeSwitch.value)) {\n        return { enabled: isTruthy(runtimeSwitch.value), key: runtimeSwitch.key, reason: \"runtime\" };\n      }\n    }\n    const globalSwitch = resolveSwitch(DEFAULT_OFF[concern]);\n    if (!holds(globalSwitch.value)) {\n      const runtime = options && typeof options.runtime === \"string\" ? options.runtime.trim().toLowerCase() : \"\";\n      if ((DEFAULT_ON_RUNTIMES[concern] || []).includes(runtime)) {\n        return { enabled: true, key: null, reason: \"default\" };\n      }\n    }\n    return { enabled: isTruthy(globalSwitch.value), key: globalSwitch.key, reason: \"global\" };\n  }\n  return { enabled: true, key: null, reason: \"default\" };\n}\n\n// The per-runtime enable switch for a default-off concern, such as\n// SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_CLAUDE_ENABLED, or null when the concern has no enable\n// switch or the runtime is not one of RUNTIMES.\nfunction runtimeEnableFlag(concern, runtime) {\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '230,290p' .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794780848706,"end":1794780850208}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780850599,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","part":{"partID":"prt_1e14663e50015mKsaxJ9JPkV74","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","messageID":"msg_1e14600ba001gYGYLUqfWmV03T","type":"tool","id":"call_3813ec51505f40a3b27d4d6d","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && echo \"=== hooks README master row? ===\"; grep -n \"SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED\\|MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\" .skilled/hooks/README.md; echo \"=== adapters reading skill-advisor switch ===\"; rg -ln \"isHookEnabled\\('skill-advisor'\\)|isHookEnabled\\(\\\"skill-advisor\\\"\\)|hookFlagDecision\\('skill-advisor'\" .skilled --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**' | head -20"},"output":"=== hooks README master row? ===\n36:Every concern except `git-message-gate` honors the master `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED` switch and its canonical `SYSTEM_<CONCERN>_DISABLED` switch. The message gate has none on purpose: the commit, PR and branch rules carry no bypass on any surface, and the place to change them is the rules block in the sk-git templates. The default is enabled, except `session-handover`, which ships on for Claude Code and off for every other runtime. The flag that decides is `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_<RUNTIME>_ENABLED` when it holds a value, where `<RUNTIME>` is `CLAUDE`, `CODEX`, `PI`, `OPENCODE`, `CURSOR`, `DEVIN` or `VIBE`, then `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED` when it holds one. With both empty or unset, only Claude Code runs it. So `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED=1` with `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_CLAUDE_ENABLED=0` is on for every runtime except Claude Code. The disable switch and the master switch still win over every enable flag. Truthy disable values are `1`, `true`, `yes`, and `on` (case-insensitive). See the kill-switch index below for the complete concern and alias inventory.\n=== adapters reading skill-advisor switch ===\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.test.cjs\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== hooks README master row? ===\n36:Every concern except `git-message-gate` honors the master `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED` switch and its canonical `SYSTEM_<CONCERN>_DISABLED` switch. The message gate has none on purpose: the commit, PR and branch rules carry no bypass on any surface, and the place to change them is the rules block in the sk-git templates. The default is enabled, except `session-handover`, which ships on for Claude Code and off for every other runtime. The flag that decides is `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_<RUNTIME>_ENABLED` when it holds a value, where `<RUNTIME>` is `CLAUDE`, `CODEX`, `PI`, `OPENCODE`, `CURSOR`, `DEVIN` or `VIBE`, then `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED` when it holds one. With both empty or unset, only Claude Code runs it. So `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED=1` with `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_CLAUDE_ENABLED=0` is on for every runtime except Claude Code. The disable switch and the master switch still win over every enable flag. Truthy disable values are `1`, `true`, `yes`, and `on` (case-insensitive). See the kill-switch index below for the complete concern and alias inventory.\n=== adapters reading skill-advisor switch ===\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts\n.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.test.cjs\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && echo \\\"=== hooks README master row? ===\\\"; grep -n \\\"SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED\\\\|MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\\\" .skilled/hooks/README.md; echo \\\"=== adapters reading skill-advisor switch ===\\\"; rg -ln \\\"isHookEnabled\\\\('skill-advisor'\\\\)|isHookEnabled\\\\(\\\\\\\"skill-advisor\\\\\\\"\\\\)|hookFlagDecision\\\\('skill-advisor'\\\" .skilled --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**' | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794780849125,"end":1794780850599}}}}
