{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780985728,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","part":{"partID":"prt_1e1487065001Y8WybuYLKzzJhe","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","messageID":"msg_1e1483d50001CeZB0jpG9ivDGv","type":"tool","id":"call_4961c5f786344fad8058fc32","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && node -e \"const h=require('./.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs'); for (const k of ['MK_HOOKS_DISABLED','MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED','MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED','MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED']) console.log(k, JSON.stringify(h.hookFlagDecision('skill-advisor',{[k]:'1'},{})))\"; echo \"=== hooks README lines ===\"; grep -n \"single source of truth\\|complete concern and alias inventory\" .skilled/hooks/README.md; grep -n \"^| \\`skill-advisor\\`\" .skilled/hooks/README.md; echo \"=== lib README §3 lines ===\"; grep -n \"shared/\\|utils/\\|skill-graph\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md | head -12; echo \"=== CP-003 control line ===\"; grep -n \"env -u SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md"},"output":"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED {\"enabled\":false,\"key\":\"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\",\"reason\":\"master\"}\nMK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED {\"enabled\":false,\"key\":\"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED\",\"reason\":\"kill\"}\nMK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED {\"enabled\":false,\"key\":\"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED\",\"reason\":\"kill\"}\nMK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED {\"enabled\":false,\"key\":\"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED\",\"reason\":\"kill\"}\n=== hooks README lines ===\n36:Every concern except `git-message-gate` honors the master `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED` switch and its canonical `SYSTEM_<CONCERN>_DISABLED` switch. The message gate has none on purpose: the commit, PR and branch rules carry no bypass on any surface, and the place to change them is the rules block in the sk-git templates. The default is enabled, except `session-handover`, which ships on for Claude Code and off for every other runtime. The flag that decides is `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_<RUNTIME>_ENABLED` when it holds a value, where `<RUNTIME>` is `CLAUDE`, `CODEX`, `PI`, `OPENCODE`, `CURSOR`, `DEVIN` or `VIBE`, then `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED` when it holds one. With both empty or unset, only Claude Code runs it. So `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED=1` with `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_CLAUDE_ENABLED=0` is on for every runtime except Claude Code. The disable switch and the master switch still win over every enable flag. Truthy disable values are `1`, `true`, `yes`, and `on` (case-insensitive). See the kill-switch index below for the complete concern and alias inventory.\n40:This table is the single source of truth for repo-authored hook kill-switch names. All concerns are wired to the shared resolver or its shell equivalent.\n44:| `skill-advisor` | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED` | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` | enabled | inject | wired |\n353:| `skill-advisor` | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered |\n=== lib README §3 lines ===\n69:+-- shared/                     # Small advisor-local shared helpers\n70:+-- utils/                      # Small utility functions\n134:+-- shared/\n135:+-- skill-graph/\n136:+-- utils/\n160:| `shared/` | Keeps advisor-local shared helpers and compatibility shims. |\n195:| `shared/` | Folder | Shared local helper modules. |\n219:- [`shared/README.md`](shared/README.md)\n=== CP-003 control line ===\n49:HOOK_FLAGS_CONFIG=/dev/null env -u SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED -u MK_HOOKS_DISABLED -u SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED -u SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED -u SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED -u MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED -u MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED -u MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED -u SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED -u SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --prompt \"help me commit my changes\" --options '{\"topK\":1}' --format json --timeout-ms 30000\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED {\"enabled\":false,\"key\":\"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\",\"reason\":\"master\"}\nMK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED {\"enabled\":false,\"key\":\"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED\",\"reason\":\"kill\"}\nMK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED {\"enabled\":false,\"key\":\"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED\",\"reason\":\"kill\"}\nMK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED {\"enabled\":false,\"key\":\"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED\",\"reason\":\"kill\"}\n=== hooks README lines ===\n36:Every concern except `git-message-gate` honors the master `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED` switch and its canonical `SYSTEM_<CONCERN>_DISABLED` switch. The message gate has none on purpose: the commit, PR and branch rules carry no bypass on any surface, and the place to change them is the rules block in the sk-git templates. The default is enabled, except `session-handover`, which ships on for Claude Code and off for every other runtime. The flag that decides is `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_<RUNTIME>_ENABLED` when it holds a value, where `<RUNTIME>` is `CLAUDE`, `CODEX`, `PI`, `OPENCODE`, `CURSOR`, `DEVIN` or `VIBE`, then `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED` when it holds one. With both empty or unset, only Claude Code runs it. So `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED=1` with `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_CLAUDE_ENABLED=0` is on for every runtime except Claude Code. The disable switch and the master switch still win over every enable flag. Truthy disable values are `1`, `true`, `yes`, and `on` (case-insensitive). See the kill-switch index below for the complete concern and alias inventory.\n40:This table is the single source of truth for repo-authored hook kill-switch names. All concerns are wired to the shared resolver or its shell equivalent.\n44:| `skill-advisor` | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED` | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` | enabled | inject | wired |\n353:| `skill-advisor` | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered |\n=== lib README §3 lines ===\n69:+-- shared/                     # Small advisor-local shared helpers\n70:+-- utils/                      # Small utility functions\n134:+-- shared/\n135:+-- skill-graph/\n136:+-- utils/\n160:| `shared/` | Keeps advisor-local shared helpers and compatibility shims. |\n195:| `shared/` | Folder | Shared local helper modules. |\n219:- [`shared/README.md`](shared/README.md)\n=== CP-003 control line ===\n49:HOOK_FLAGS_CONFIG=/dev/null env -u SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED -u MK_HOOKS_DISABLED -u SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED -u SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED -u SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED -u MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED -u MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED -u MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED -u SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED -u SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --prompt \"help me commit my changes\" --options '{\"topK\":1}' --format json --timeout-ms 30000\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && node -e \\\"const h=require('./.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs'); for (const k of ['MK_HOOKS_DISABLED','MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED','MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED','MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED']) console.log(k, JSON.stringify(h.hookFlagDecision('skill-advisor',{[k]:'1'},{})))\\\"; echo \\\"=== hooks README lines ===\\\"; grep -n \\\"single source of truth\\\\|complete concern and alias inventory\\\" .skilled/hooks/README.md; grep -n \\\"^| \\\\`skill-advisor\\\\`\\\" .skilled/hooks/README.md; echo \\\"=== lib README §3 lines ===\\\"; grep -n \\\"shared/\\\\|utils/\\\\|skill-graph\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md | head -12; echo \\\"=== CP-003 control line ===\\\"; grep -n \\\"env -u SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794780983397,"end":1794780985728}}}}
