{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781083123,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","part":{"partID":"prt_1e1493f89002Hb9nShcEXM1ZoX","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","messageID":"msg_1e148f710001Ap7mn74pzskKYJ","type":"tool","id":"call_ee495d905ab74ad183dab3bb","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 1: Correctness and Traceability of the Pass-Five Kill-Switch Fixes\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Run: `fanout-kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b-1794780590351-ezt1v0`\n- Mode: review; target agent: `@deep-review`; execution: single review iteration\n- Lineage: `kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b`; confirming-round-`5b` area `kill-switch-cli`\n- Operator review focus: confirming round `5b`; read `review-brief-5b.txt` first; review the `kill-switch-cli` files plus docs that describe them; every finding carries `file:line` and a concrete input; check that the kill-switch names agree in code and docs and that docs agree with code; holdout hygiene is counts-only.\n- Dimension this iteration: D1 correctness and D3 traceability. This is a confirming round, so the behavior claim and the doc that states it are read together: each of the six confirmed pass-five P2 findings for this area is checked against the fix at `d21dbc1cafe`, then the docs that describe the same switch set are compared with the resolver.\n- Sources read this iteration: `review-brief-5b.txt`, `review-scope-5b.txt`, `review-focus-5b.txt`, `verify-5/report.md`, `032-review-pass-five-remediation/plan.md` (D13), `deep-review-strategy.md`, `deep-review-config.json`, `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/review-core.md`, the diff `2a1a42263cc..d21dbc1cafe` for the five scope paths, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:70-80`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md:39-60`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:54-140`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts:9-15,100-175`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts:13-22,145-160,215-245`, `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:38-106,230-285`, `.skilled/hooks/shared/env-aliases.cjs:1-50`, `.skilled/hooks/README.md:30-50`, `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example:1-20`, and the pass-five `kill-switch-cli-5` iterations as prior context.\n- Steer channel: `steer.md` does not exist in the lineage directory; no lead ruling was available for this iteration.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:70-80` (fix diff plus the surrounding switch table)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md:1-60,75-90`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:54-140`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts:9-15,100-175`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts:13-22,145-160,215-245`\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:38-106,230-285` (context: the resolver the docs describe)\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/env-aliases.cjs:1-50` (context: the `MK_` bridge that makes the alias names work)\n- `.skilled/hooks/README.md:30-50` (context: the doc that calls itself the single source of truth)\n- `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example:1-20` (context: the doc that defers the canonical index to `hooks/README.md`)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/` (directory listing at `d21dbc1cafe`)\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The hook kill-switch index still omits the four `MK_` aliases the resolver honors and this commit added to ENV-REFERENCE** -- `.skilled/hooks/README.md:44` -- The row for `skill-advisor` lists four aliases (`SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`) and the file has no master row, so `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED`, `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`, `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED` and `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` appear nowhere while the table calls itself \"the single source of truth for repo-authored hook kill-switch names\" `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/README.md:40]` and the paragraph above it points at \"the complete concern and alias inventory\" `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/README.md:36]`. The resolver honors all four: `MASTER_ALIASES = [\"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\"]` is checked in the same master loop as the canonical name `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:38-41,256-258]`, and the three `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_*` names sit in `LEGACY_ALIASES['skill-advisor']` `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:64-78]`. This commit added exactly those names to the ENV-REFERENCE rows `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:74-75]`, and `hook-flags.env.example` names `hooks/README.md` as the canonical index `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example:12-15]`, so the two index tables now disagree. Pass-five iteration 2 named this table as the second site of the same confirmed drift `[SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/iterations/iteration-002.md:38]`; the fix commit changed only the ENV-REFERENCE site.\n- Case: an operator exports `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1`; the advisor abstains, yet the table they were told is the complete inventory does not list that name, and it also does not say that `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED=1` silences every hook.\n- Evidence: a read-only probe of the shared resolver, no daemon and no file write, printed `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED {\"enabled\":false,\"key\":\"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\",\"reason\":\"master\"}` and `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`, `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` each `{\"enabled\":false,...,\"reason\":\"kill\"}`. `rg -n \"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR|MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\" .skilled/hooks/README.md` returns no row and no alias column hit.\n- User impact: the file advertised as the one place to look for kill-switch names under-reports the set by four names, including the master alias that switches off every repo-authored hook.\n- Finding class: class-of-bug\n- Scope proof: compared the four doc copies of the switch list against `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts:74-81]`. `ENV-REFERENCE.md:74-75` and `global-disable-flag.md:49` now carry all ten; `hooks/README.md:44` carries six of ten (one canonical, four aliases, one master canonical in prose) and omits every `MK_` name. The generator-side fix is one list in one place, not four hand-edited tables.\n- Affected surface hints: [\"hook kill-switch index\", \"ENV-REFERENCE switch table\", \"CP-003 control command\", \"resolver alias constants\"]\n- Recommendation: add `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED` beside the master switch in the prose at `:36` and the three `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_*` names to the alias column at `:44`, or generate both index tables from the resolver's `MASTER_ALIASES` and `LEGACY_ALIASES`.\n\n2. **The package topology omits `skill-graph/` while the directory tree and the directory itself have it** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:69` -- Section 3 `PACKAGE TOPOLOGY` jumps from `shared/` to `utils/` and never names `skill-graph/`, although section 4 `DIRECTORY TREE` lists it `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:135]` and the folder is on disk `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/]`. The fix for the pass-five finding added the nine missing folders to section 4 and left section 3 one folder short of the fourteen that exist.\n- Case: a reader who opens the package topology to find where the graph code lives sees thirteen folders, and `lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.js`, which the launcher test imports for `initDb` and the lease uses, has no row in that section.\n- Evidence: `git ls-tree --name-only d21dbc1cafe .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/` prints fourteen folders and twenty-two flat modules. Section 4 lists all fourteen folders and all twenty-two modules; section 3 lists thirteen folders and five of the twenty-two modules `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:57-76,98-136]`.\n- User impact: the topology map, which is the only section that carries a one-line purpose per folder, silently drops the folder that owns the skill graph.\n- Finding class: instance-only\n- Scope proof: compared every entry of the `d21dbc1cafe` tree against both sections. Section 4 matches 14/14 folders and 22/22 modules; section 3 matches 13/14 folders. No other section claims a folder inventory `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:150-200]`.\n- Affected surface hints: [\"lib package topology\", \"lib directory tree\"]\n- Recommendation: add `+-- skill-graph/   # Skill graph database, lease and rebuild helpers` between `shared/` and `utils/`.\n- Downgrade trigger: if section 3 is meant as a curated overview rather than a complete folder map, this is optional polish; the five-flat-module list suggests curation, but the folder list was complete for every other folder before this commit.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- `spec_code`: pass. The packet's confirming brief asks whether the kill-switch names agree in code and docs. The resolver declares one master flag, one master alias, one canonical concern flag and seven legacy aliases `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:38-78]`; `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` composes exactly those ten names `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts:74-81]`; `ENV-REFERENCE.md:74-75` and `global-disable-flag.md:49` now carry the same ten, and `launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts` and `skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts` both read the constant instead of restating it. The one remaining disagreement is `hooks/README.md:44`, reported as P2 above.\n- `checklist_evidence`: partial. The parent packet holds no checklist row that names this area; the confirming brief is the checklist used here. Its two `kill-switch-cli` items (names agree in code and docs; docs agree with code) are both covered, with two residual P2 doc gaps recorded against them rather than a silent pass.\n- `feature_catalog_code` and `playbook_capability`: exercised by reading CP-003's control command against the resolver and the two test fixtures; the overlay rows are marked pass for this iteration below.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `cli-surface`: the CLI disable loop now parameterizes all ten names, including the three `MK_` names the previous round filtered out `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts:219]`. For an `MK_` name the assertion is one abstain reason with the fixed prefix, because the load-time bridge rewrites the name before the resolver reads it `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts:230-235]` `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/env-aliases.cjs:31-49]`; a non-`MK_` name still pins the exact reason.\n- `daemon-launcher`: the child-env fixture now builds its env from `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` and asserts the extracted list has ten entries before asserting the filtered child env `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts:129-143]`. A constant that collapsed to an empty array would fail the size assertion rather than pass an empty fixture.\n- `manual scenario`: CP-003's control command unsets all ten names before its control call `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md:49]`. The set is complete: `DEFAULT_OFF` names only `session-handover`, so the advisor has no enable switch to carry a disable value `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:104-106,270-283]`.\n- `env-index`: `ENV-REFERENCE.md:74` now states the master alias, and `:75` lists the seven skill-advisor aliases; both match `MASTER_ALIASES` and `LEGACY_ALIASES['skill-advisor']` name for name `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:38-78]`.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- `ENV-REFERENCE.md:75`'s Source cell now names the CLI and the daemon handler, which is what the confirming report asked for, but the Vibe adapter is a third reader of the same switch: `buildAdvisorPart` defaults `isEnabled` to `isHookEnabled` and calls it for `skill-advisor` `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs:212-222]`. That file is `vibe-hooks-doctor` area in the same confirming round (`review-scope-5b.txt:10`), so it is recorded here as a cross-area note rather than raised again under a Source-cell finding that the verifier scoped to the CLI and the handler.\n- The fix range `2a1a42263cc..d21dbc1cafe` is not HEAD (`9c031900e44`). Every line cited above was read in the working tree and cross-checked with the diff, and none of the five scope files changed after `d21dbc1cafe`: the diff stat for the five paths and the working-tree content agree.\n- `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` is empty when `hook-flags.cjs` cannot be found `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts:53-81]`. In that state both tests fail loudly (the size assertion and the empty parameter list) instead of passing a narrower fixture, so the fail-open resolver cannot turn into a silent test pass. Recorded, not a finding.\n- The pass-five lineage's ruled-out direction \"the README's folder list is a file list and must name every folder\" is respected: section 3 is treated as the folder map, which is why the missing folder is reported, and the five-flat-module subset is not reported.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- **`iter2-P2-env-alias-column` is fixed.** `ENV-REFERENCE.md:74` now reads \"Alias: `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED`\" and `:75` lists the seven legacy names. Compared name for name against `MASTER_ALIASES` and `LEGACY_ALIASES['skill-advisor']`: no omission, no extra name `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:38-78]` `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:74-75]`.\n- **`iter2-P2-env-source-column` is fixed.** The Source cell names the CLI and the handler in addition to the two adapters `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:75]`; the CLI reaches `disabledRecommendOutput` before any daemon path and the handler reaches it before `computeRecommendationOutput` `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts:145-160]`.\n- **`iter2-P2-cp003-control-aliases` is fixed.** The control command unsets ten names, which is the complete env switch set: one master flag, one master alias, one canonical concern flag and seven legacy aliases `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md:49]`.\n- **`iter3-P2-launcher-switch-fixture` is fixed.** The fixture is derived from `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS`, asserts ten names, and still asserts the exact filtered child env `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts:129-143]`.\n- **`iter3-P2-cli-mk-alias-filter` is fixed.** The filter and its load-order comment are gone; all ten names run, the `MK_` reason is deliberately loose and documented in a comment, and every other name keeps the exact-reason assertion `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts:218-238]`.\n- **`iter3-P2-lib-readme-tree` is fixed for the section the finding named.** Section 4 now lists twenty-two flat modules and fourteen folders, matching `git ls-tree` at `d21dbc1cafe` exactly `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:98-136]`.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **The CLI loop's loose `MK_` assertion can hide a wrong switch.** `switchEnv` deletes every name in `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` before setting the one under test `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts:151-156]`, and the loop also asserts one reason, the fixed prefix, `ADVISOR_DISABLED`, `freshness: unavailable` and zero daemon calls, so the only switch present is the one under test. The looseness covers the load-time rename, not an unset fixture.\n- **The launcher size assertion hides a name added to the constant.** It fails closed instead: a new name makes `toHaveLength(10)` fail and forces the fixture to be re-read, which is the guard the comment claims `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts:137-139]`.\n- **The CP-003 control command can still start disabled through a flags file.** The command sets `HOOK_FLAGS_CONFIG=/dev/null`, so the file config is empty, and the ten env names are unset `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md:49]`.\n- **`MK_HOOKS_DISABLED` is a second master alias that the resolver ignores.** The probe returns `reason: \"master\"`, so it is honored; the omission is in the doc, not the code `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:256-258]`.\n- **A tracked dotenv, holdout or prompt file is read by any reviewed file.** No reviewed file opens `command-prompts.jsonl`, `holdout-prompts.jsonl` or `behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl`; the switch docs name no prompt text. Holdout hygiene holds for this area.\n- **The five scope files changed after the fix commit.** The diff and the working tree agree for all five paths; no post-`d21dbc1cafe` edit changes a cited line.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security and maintainability (D2, D4)\n- Focus area: re-read the switch paths the docs promise for a bypass the fix could have introduced: the `MK_` bridge order, the CLI/handler abstain before I/O, and the launcher allowlist. Then judge maintainability: the ten-name list now exists in four hand-maintained places (resolver constants, `ENV-REFERENCE.md`, `hooks/README.md`, CP-003) and the module map in two.\n- Reason: iteration 1 confirms five of the six fixes and leaves two P2 doc gaps; the untested half of the round is whether the widened fixtures or the widened doc claims widened the attack surface or the change cost.\n- Rotation status: D1 and D3 covered; D2 and D4 remain.\n- Required evidence: exact resolver and reader line numbers, the child-env allowlist, and the four copies of the alias list counted rather than inferred.\n- Recovery note: none.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-001.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-001.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Iteration 1: Correctness and Traceability of the Pass-Five Kill-Switch Fixes\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Run: `fanout-kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b-1794780590351-ezt1v0`\\n- Mode: review; target agent: `@deep-review`; execution: single review iteration\\n- Lineage: `kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b`; confirming-round-`5b` area `kill-switch-cli`\\n- Operator review focus: confirming round `5b`; read `review-brief-5b.txt` first; review the `kill-switch-cli` files plus docs that describe them; every finding carries `file:line` and a concrete input; check that the kill-switch names agree in code and docs and that docs agree with code; holdout hygiene is counts-only.\\n- Dimension this iteration: D1 correctness and D3 traceability. This is a confirming round, so the behavior claim and the doc that states it are read together: each of the six confirmed pass-five P2 findings for this area is checked against the fix at `d21dbc1cafe`, then the docs that describe the same switch set are compared with the resolver.\\n- Sources read this iteration: `review-brief-5b.txt`, `review-scope-5b.txt`, `review-focus-5b.txt`, `verify-5/report.md`, `032-review-pass-five-remediation/plan.md` (D13), `deep-review-strategy.md`, `deep-review-config.json`, `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/review-core.md`, the diff `2a1a42263cc..d21dbc1cafe` for the five scope paths, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:70-80`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md:39-60`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:54-140`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts:9-15,100-175`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts:13-22,145-160,215-245`, `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:38-106,230-285`, `.skilled/hooks/shared/env-aliases.cjs:1-50`, `.skilled/hooks/README.md:30-50`, `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example:1-20`, and the pass-five `kill-switch-cli-5` iterations as prior context.\\n- Steer channel: `steer.md` does not exist in the lineage directory; no lead ruling was available for this iteration.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:70-80` (fix diff plus the surrounding switch table)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md:1-60,75-90`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:54-140`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts:9-15,100-175`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts:13-22,145-160,215-245`\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:38-106,230-285` (context: the resolver the docs describe)\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/env-aliases.cjs:1-50` (context: the `MK_` bridge that makes the alias names work)\\n- `.skilled/hooks/README.md:30-50` (context: the doc that calls itself the single source of truth)\\n- `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example:1-20` (context: the doc that defers the canonical index to `hooks/README.md`)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/` (directory listing at `d21dbc1cafe`)\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **The hook kill-switch index still omits the four `MK_` aliases the resolver honors and this commit added to ENV-REFERENCE** -- `.skilled/hooks/README.md:44` -- The row for `skill-advisor` lists four aliases (`SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`) and the file has no master row, so `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED`, `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`, `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED` and `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` appear nowhere while the table calls itself \\\"the single source of truth for repo-authored hook kill-switch names\\\" `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/README.md:40]` and the paragraph above it points at \\\"the complete concern and alias inventory\\\" `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/README.md:36]`. The resolver honors all four: `MASTER_ALIASES = [\\\"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\\\"]` is checked in the same master loop as the canonical name `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:38-41,256-258]`, and the three `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_*` names sit in `LEGACY_ALIASES['skill-advisor']` `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:64-78]`. This commit added exactly those names to the ENV-REFERENCE rows `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:74-75]`, and `hook-flags.env.example` names `hooks/README.md` as the canonical index `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example:12-15]`, so the two index tables now disagree. Pass-five iteration 2 named this table as the second site of the same confirmed drift `[SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/iterations/iteration-002.md:38]`; the fix commit changed only the ENV-REFERENCE site.\\n- Case: an operator exports `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1`; the advisor abstains, yet the table they were told is the complete inventory does not list that name, and it also does not say that `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED=1` silences every hook.\\n- Evidence: a read-only probe of the shared resolver, no daemon and no file write, printed `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED {\\\"enabled\\\":false,\\\"key\\\":\\\"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"master\\\"}` and `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`, `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` each `{\\\"enabled\\\":false,...,\\\"reason\\\":\\\"kill\\\"}`. `rg -n \\\"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR|MK_HOOKS_DISABLED\\\" .skilled/hooks/README.md` returns no row and no alias column hit.\\n- User impact: the file advertised as the one place to look for kill-switch names under-reports the set by four names, including the master alias that switches off every repo-authored hook.\\n- Finding class: class-of-bug\\n- Scope proof: compared the four doc copies of the switch list against `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts:74-81]`. `ENV-REFERENCE.md:74-75` and `global-disable-flag.md:49` now carry all ten; `hooks/README.md:44` carries six of ten (one canonical, four aliases, one master canonical in prose) and omits every `MK_` name. The generator-side fix is one list in one place, not four hand-edited tables.\\n- Affected surface hints: [\\\"hook kill-switch index\\\", \\\"ENV-REFERENCE switch table\\\", \\\"CP-003 control command\\\", \\\"resolver alias constants\\\"]\\n- Recommendation: add `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED` beside the master switch in the prose at `:36` and the three `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_*` names to the alias column at `:44`, or generate both index tables from the resolver's `MASTER_ALIASES` and `LEGACY_ALIASES`.\\n\\n2. **The package topology omits `skill-graph/` while the directory tree and the directory itself have it** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:69` -- Section 3 `PACKAGE TOPOLOGY` jumps from `shared/` to `utils/` and never names `skill-graph/`, although section 4 `DIRECTORY TREE` lists it `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:135]` and the folder is on disk `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/]`. The fix for the pass-five finding added the nine missing folders to section 4 and left section 3 one folder short of the fourteen that exist.\\n- Case: a reader who opens the package topology to find where the graph code lives sees thirteen folders, and `lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.js`, which the launcher test imports for `initDb` and the lease uses, has no row in that section.\\n- Evidence: `git ls-tree --name-only d21dbc1cafe .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/` prints fourteen folders and twenty-two flat modules. Section 4 lists all fourteen folders and all twenty-two modules; section 3 lists thirteen folders and five of the twenty-two modules `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:57-76,98-136]`.\\n- User impact: the topology map, which is the only section that carries a one-line purpose per folder, silently drops the folder that owns the skill graph.\\n- Finding class: instance-only\\n- Scope proof: compared every entry of the `d21dbc1cafe` tree against both sections. Section 4 matches 14/14 folders and 22/22 modules; section 3 matches 13/14 folders. No other section claims a folder inventory `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:150-200]`.\\n- Affected surface hints: [\\\"lib package topology\\\", \\\"lib directory tree\\\"]\\n- Recommendation: add `+-- skill-graph/   # Skill graph database, lease and rebuild helpers` between `shared/` and `utils/`.\\n- Downgrade trigger: if section 3 is meant as a curated overview rather than a complete folder map, this is optional polish; the five-flat-module list suggests curation, but the folder list was complete for every other folder before this commit.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- `spec_code`: pass. The packet's confirming brief asks whether the kill-switch names agree in code and docs. The resolver declares one master flag, one master alias, one canonical concern flag and seven legacy aliases `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:38-78]`; `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` composes exactly those ten names `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts:74-81]`; `ENV-REFERENCE.md:74-75` and `global-disable-flag.md:49` now carry the same ten, and `launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts` and `skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts` both read the constant instead of restating it. The one remaining disagreement is `hooks/README.md:44`, reported as P2 above.\\n- `checklist_evidence`: partial. The parent packet holds no checklist row that names this area; the confirming brief is the checklist used here. Its two `kill-switch-cli` items (names agree in code and docs; docs agree with code) are both covered, with two residual P2 doc gaps recorded against them rather than a silent pass.\\n- `feature_catalog_code` and `playbook_capability`: exercised by reading CP-003's control command against the resolver and the two test fixtures; the overlay rows are marked pass for this iteration below.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `cli-surface`: the CLI disable loop now parameterizes all ten names, including the three `MK_` names the previous round filtered out `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts:219]`. For an `MK_` name the assertion is one abstain reason with the fixed prefix, because the load-time bridge rewrites the name before the resolver reads it `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts:230-235]` `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/env-aliases.cjs:31-49]`; a non-`MK_` name still pins the exact reason.\\n- `daemon-launcher`: the child-env fixture now builds its env from `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` and asserts the extracted list has ten entries before asserting the filtered child env `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts:129-143]`. A constant that collapsed to an empty array would fail the size assertion rather than pass an empty fixture.\\n- `manual scenario`: CP-003's control command unsets all ten names before its control call `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md:49]`. The set is complete: `DEFAULT_OFF` names only `session-handover`, so the advisor has no enable switch to carry a disable value `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:104-106,270-283]`.\\n- `env-index`: `ENV-REFERENCE.md:74` now states the master alias, and `:75` lists the seven skill-advisor aliases; both match `MASTER_ALIASES` and `LEGACY_ALIASES['skill-advisor']` name for name `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:38-78]`.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- `ENV-REFERENCE.md:75`'s Source cell now names the CLI and the daemon handler, which is what the confirming report asked for, but the Vibe adapter is a third reader of the same switch: `buildAdvisorPart` defaults `isEnabled` to `isHookEnabled` and calls it for `skill-advisor` `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs:212-222]`. That file is `vibe-hooks-doctor` area in the same confirming round (`review-scope-5b.txt:10`), so it is recorded here as a cross-area note rather than raised again under a Source-cell finding that the verifier scoped to the CLI and the handler.\\n- The fix range `2a1a42263cc..d21dbc1cafe` is not HEAD (`9c031900e44`). Every line cited above was read in the working tree and cross-checked with the diff, and none of the five scope files changed after `d21dbc1cafe`: the diff stat for the five paths and the working-tree content agree.\\n- `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` is empty when `hook-flags.cjs` cannot be found `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts:53-81]`. In that state both tests fail loudly (the size assertion and the empty parameter list) instead of passing a narrower fixture, so the fail-open resolver cannot turn into a silent test pass. Recorded, not a finding.\\n- The pass-five lineage's ruled-out direction \\\"the README's folder list is a file list and must name every folder\\\" is respected: section 3 is treated as the folder map, which is why the missing folder is reported, and the five-flat-module subset is not reported.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- **`iter2-P2-env-alias-column` is fixed.** `ENV-REFERENCE.md:74` now reads \\\"Alias: `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED`\\\" and `:75` lists the seven legacy names. Compared name for name against `MASTER_ALIASES` and `LEGACY_ALIASES['skill-advisor']`: no omission, no extra name `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:38-78]` `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:74-75]`.\\n- **`iter2-P2-env-source-column` is fixed.** The Source cell names the CLI and the handler in addition to the two adapters `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:75]`; the CLI reaches `disabledRecommendOutput` before any daemon path and the handler reaches it before `computeRecommendationOutput` `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts:145-160]`.\\n- **`iter2-P2-cp003-control-aliases` is fixed.** The control command unsets ten names, which is the complete env switch set: one master flag, one master alias, one canonical concern flag and seven legacy aliases `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md:49]`.\\n- **`iter3-P2-launcher-switch-fixture` is fixed.** The fixture is derived from `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS`, asserts ten names, and still asserts the exact filtered child env `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts:129-143]`.\\n- **`iter3-P2-cli-mk-alias-filter` is fixed.** The filter and its load-order comment are gone; all ten names run, the `MK_` reason is deliberately loose and documented in a comment, and every other name keeps the exact-reason assertion `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts:218-238]`.\\n- **`iter3-P2-lib-readme-tree` is fixed for the section the finding named.** Section 4 now lists twenty-two flat modules and fourteen folders, matching `git ls-tree` at `d21dbc1cafe` exactly `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:98-136]`.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **The CLI loop's loose `MK_` assertion can hide a wrong switch.** `switchEnv` deletes every name in `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` before setting the one under test `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts:151-156]`, and the loop also asserts one reason, the fixed prefix, `ADVISOR_DISABLED`, `freshness: unavailable` and zero daemon calls, so the only switch present is the one under test. The looseness covers the load-time rename, not an unset fixture.\\n- **The launcher size assertion hides a name added to the constant.** It fails closed instead: a new name makes `toHaveLength(10)` fail and forces the fixture to be re-read, which is the guard the comment claims `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts:137-139]`.\\n- **The CP-003 control command can still start disabled through a flags file.** The command sets `HOOK_FLAGS_CONFIG=/dev/null`, so the file config is empty, and the ten env names are unset `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md:49]`.\\n- **`MK_HOOKS_DISABLED` is a second master alias that the resolver ignores.** The probe returns `reason: \\\"master\\\"`, so it is honored; the omission is in the doc, not the code `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:256-258]`.\\n- **A tracked dotenv, holdout or prompt file is read by any reviewed file.** No reviewed file opens `command-prompts.jsonl`, `holdout-prompts.jsonl` or `behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl`; the switch docs name no prompt text. Holdout hygiene holds for this area.\\n- **The five scope files changed after the fix commit.** The diff and the working tree agree for all five paths; no post-`d21dbc1cafe` edit changes a cited line.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: security and maintainability (D2, D4)\\n- Focus area: re-read the switch paths the docs promise for a bypass the fix could have introduced: the `MK_` bridge order, the CLI/handler abstain before I/O, and the launcher allowlist. Then judge maintainability: the ten-name list now exists in four hand-maintained places (resolver constants, `ENV-REFERENCE.md`, `hooks/README.md`, CP-003) and the module map in two.\\n- Reason: iteration 1 confirms five of the six fixes and leaves two P2 doc gaps; the untested half of the round is whether the widened fixtures or the widened doc claims widened the attack surface or the change cost.\\n- Rotation status: D1 and D3 covered; D2 and D4 remain.\\n- Required evidence: exact resolver and reader line numbers, the child-env allowlist, and the four copies of the alias list counted rather than inferred.\\n- Recovery note: none.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794781036425,"end":1794781083123}}}}
