{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781096501,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","part":{"partID":"prt_1e14a1b47001c7srm0eeE5Hwgp","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","messageID":"msg_1e149fa63001KzZoNrtQB9CRuA","type":"tool","id":"call_4b44e84a63654868bd525c3d","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"## 6. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 7. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]","newString":"## 6. WHAT WORKED\n- Reading the fix diff beside the working tree for the five scope paths confirmed the fix range is not HEAD but none of the five files moved after it, so the citations stay valid (iteration 1).\n- Comparing the resolver's `MASTER_ALIASES` and `LEGACY_ALIASES['skill-advisor']` name for name against the two index tables found the one table the fix did not patch instead of a guessed drift (iteration 1).\n- Running a read-only probe of `hookFlagDecision` for the four `MK_` names turned \"the doc omits them\" into \"the doc omits names that observably disable the advisor\" (iteration 1).\n- Diffing `git ls-tree` at the fix commit against both README trees proved section 4 complete and section 3 one folder short without a second directory scan (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 7. WHAT FAILED\n- Reading `ENV-REFERENCE.md:74-75` alone made the alias fix look complete; the canonical index its own header defers to still disagreed (iteration 1).\n- Treating the pass-five verifier's fix column as the full scope of the confirmed finding hid the second site the pass-five iteration had already named (iteration 1)."},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -70,14 +70,18 @@\n \n ---\n \n ## 6. WHAT WORKED\n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Reading the fix diff beside the working tree for the five scope paths confirmed the fix range is not HEAD but none of the five files moved after it, so the citations stay valid (iteration 1).\n+- Comparing the resolver's `MASTER_ALIASES` and `LEGACY_ALIASES['skill-advisor']` name for name against the two index tables found the one table the fix did not patch instead of a guessed drift (iteration 1).\n+- Running a read-only probe of `hookFlagDecision` for the four `MK_` names turned \"the doc omits them\" into \"the doc omits names that observably disable the advisor\" (iteration 1).\n+- Diffing `git ls-tree` at the fix commit against both README trees proved section 4 complete and section 3 one folder short without a second directory scan (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n ## 7. WHAT FAILED\n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Reading `ENV-REFERENCE.md:74-75` alone made the alias fix look complete; the canonical index its own header defers to still disagreed (iteration 1).\n+- Treating the pass-five verifier's fix column as the full scope of the confirmed finding hid the second site the pass-five iteration had already named (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":6,"deletions":2}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md\",\"oldString\":\"## 6. WHAT WORKED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. WHAT FAILED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\",\"newString\":\"## 6. WHAT WORKED\\n- Reading the fix diff beside the working tree for the five scope paths confirmed the fix range is not HEAD but none of the five files moved after it, so the citations stay valid (iteration 1).\\n- Comparing the resolver's `MASTER_ALIASES` and `LEGACY_ALIASES['skill-advisor']` name for name against the two index tables found the one table the fix did not patch instead of a guessed drift (iteration 1).\\n- Running a read-only probe of `hookFlagDecision` for the four `MK_` names turned \\\"the doc omits them\\\" into \\\"the doc omits names that observably disable the advisor\\\" (iteration 1).\\n- Diffing `git ls-tree` at the fix commit against both README trees proved section 4 complete and section 3 one folder short without a second directory scan (iteration 1).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. WHAT FAILED\\n- Reading `ENV-REFERENCE.md:74-75` alone made the alias fix look complete; the canonical index its own header defers to still disagreed (iteration 1).\\n- Treating the pass-five verifier's fix column as the full scope of the confirmed finding hid the second site the pass-five iteration had already named (iteration 1).\"}"},"time":{"start":1794781092679,"end":1794781096501}}}}
