{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781110246,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","part":{"partID":"prt_1e14a38d0002jk7CcHu7iemdFH","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","messageID":"msg_1e14a2eed001dOKOgYM0Ht44W3","type":"tool","id":"call_351304a756b745a6afc052cf","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: security and maintainability (D2, D4)\n- Focus area: re-read the switch paths the docs promise for a bypass the fix could have introduced (the `MK_` bridge order, the CLI/handler abstain before I/O, the launcher allowlist), then judge maintainability across the four hand-maintained copies of the ten-name list and the two module-map sections.\n- Reason: iteration 1 confirms five of the six fixes and leaves two P2 doc gaps; the untested half of the round is whether the widened fixtures or widened doc claims widened the attack surface or the change cost.\n- Rotation status: D1 and D3 covered; D2 and D4 remain.\n- Required evidence: exact resolver and reader line numbers, the child-env allowlist, and the four copies of the alias list counted rather than inferred.\n- Recovery note: none.","oldString":"## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: correctness and traceability (D1, D3)\n- Focus area: read `review-brief-5b.txt`, `verify-5/report.md`, and the diff for the five `kill-switch-cli` paths, then confirm the six pass-five fixes for this area: the `ENV-REFERENCE.md` alias and source columns, the CP-003 control command's ten names, the launcher child-env fixture, the CLI disable loop, and the `runtime/lib` module map.\n- Reason: this is a confirming round; the first pass must establish whether each confirmed P2 is actually fixed before the round can widen.\n- Rotation status: D1 and D3 run first; D2 and D4 remain.\n- Required evidence: exact doc lines, the resolver constants (`MASTER_ALIASES`, `LEGACY_ALIASES`, `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS`), the reader line numbers, and the directory listing the module map claims.\n- Recovery note: none.","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -106,13 +106,13 @@\n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n-- Dimension: correctness and traceability (D1, D3)\n-- Focus area: read `review-brief-5b.txt`, `verify-5/report.md`, and the diff for the five `kill-switch-cli` paths, then confirm the six pass-five fixes for this area: the `ENV-REFERENCE.md` alias and source columns, the CP-003 control command's ten names, the launcher child-env fixture, the CLI disable loop, and the `runtime/lib` module map.\n-- Reason: this is a confirming round; the first pass must establish whether each confirmed P2 is actually fixed before the round can widen.\n-- Rotation status: D1 and D3 run first; D2 and D4 remain.\n-- Required evidence: exact doc lines, the resolver constants (`MASTER_ALIASES`, `LEGACY_ALIASES`, `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS`), the reader line numbers, and the directory listing the module map claims.\n+- Dimension: security and maintainabili