rvably disable the advisor\" (iteration 1).\n - Diffing `git ls-tree` at the fix commit against both README trees proved section 4 complete and section 3 one folder short without a second directory scan (iteration 1).\n - Reading the launcher allowlist and the test scope together proved the ten-name fixture cannot leak a switch into the daemon child env and cannot be bent by a developer's flags file (iteration 2).\n - Counting the three prompt files with `wc -l` kept the holdout rule while giving the report a real row count (iteration 2).\n+- Pinning each scope path's last-touching commit proved the reviewed content is the fix state and that the fix landed at `d0f605b42f8` rather than the range tip (iteration 3).\n \n ---\n \n ## 7. WHAT FAILED\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"- Counting the three prompt files with `wc -l` kept the holdout rule while giving the report a real row count (iteration 2).\\n- Pinning each scope path's last-touching commit proved the reviewed content is the fix state and that the fix landed at `d0f605b42f8` rather than the range tip (iteration 3).\",\"oldString\":\"- Counting the three prompt files with `wc -l` kept the holdout rule while giving the report a real row count (iteration 2).\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794781438372,"end":1794781441450}}}}
