{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781464395,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","part":{"partID":"prt_1e14fc595001Sd3awxrcLmRqtc","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","messageID":"msg_1e14f983c001J0ZczxZEqxDM24","type":"tool","id":"call_419a5c728974446695e7fd90","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":70,"offset":1925,"path":".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml, lines 1925-1994\n1925:              - status: active | duplicate | upgraded | downgraded | contested | resolved_false_positive\n1926:              - Record first_seen, upgraded_in, previous_severity for severity changes\n1927:              - Record dimensions array reflecting all dimensions that emitted this finding\n1928:           5. Resolve contradictions:\n1929:              - Findings marked contested across iterations → referee pass\n1930:              - Determine final severity and status\n1931:           6. Count only 'active' findings for totals\n1932:         outputs:\n1933:           - finding_registry: \"Deduplicated list of all findings with metadata\"\n1934:           - active_p0: \"Count of active P0 findings\"\n1935:           - active_p1: \"Count of active P1 findings\"\n1936:           - active_p2: \"Count of active P2 findings\"\n1937: \n1938:       step_adversarial_selfcheck:\n1939:         action: \"Final adversarial self-check on all P0 and P1 findings\"\n1940:         algorithm: |\n1941:           For each active P0/P1 finding:\n1942:             1. Hunter: Re-verify finding against source code (re-read file:line)\n1943:             2. Skeptic: Challenge severity — is this really P0/P1? Could it be P2?\n1944:             3. Referee: Final call — confirm, downgrade, or mark false_positive\n1945:           Update finding_registry with adjudicated results.\n1946: \n1947:       step_emit_resource_map:\n1948:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n1949:         action: \"Emit {state_paths.resource_map_output} from converged review deltas unless config.resource_map.emit is false\"\n1950:         dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n1951:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors --emit-resource-map\"\n1952:         read:\n1953:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1954:           - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n1955:         write:\n1956:           - \"{state_paths.resource_map_output}\"\n1957:         guarantee: \"Reducer skips cleanly when config.resource_map.emit == false and writes a deterministic resource-map when enabled.\"\n1958:         note: \"A fan-out root has no root state log before closeout, so the root reducer would fail on the missing file. Each lineage emits its own map, so the report names the ones that exist at {artifact_dir}/lineages/*/resource-map.md.\"\n1959: \n1960:       step_resource_map_coverage_gate:\n1961:         action: \"If resource_map_present, compute the Resource Map Coverage Gate synthesis inputs; otherwise preserve the skip note\"\n1962:         note: \"Cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md. Report touched entries, untouched entries split into expected-by-scope vs gap, and implementation paths absent from the map. Findings raised here use category resource-map-coverage with severity calibrated to the gate outcome.\"\n1963: \n1964:       step_compile_review_report:\n1965:         action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n1966:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1967:         instructions: |\n1968:           Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n1969: \n1970:           1. **Executive Summary**\n1971:              - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n1972:              - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n1973:              - P0/P1/P2 counts (active only)\n1974:              - Review scope summary\n1975:              - Operator review focus: config.reviewFocus verbatim, or omit this line when it is null\n1976: \n1977:           2. **Planning Trigger**\n1978:              - State whether `/speckit:plan` is required\n1979:              - Include a fenced `json` block labeled `Planning Packet`\n1980:              - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n1981:              - Build `activeFindings`, `findingClasses`, and `affectedSurfacesSeed` from reducer-owned state plus iteration JSONL `findingDetails`; if a field is missing, mark it `UNKNOWN` instead of inferring it from prose\n1982: \n1983:           3. **Active Finding Registry**\n1984:              - Unified registry for active P0/P1/P2 findings\n1985:              - For each: ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints\n1986: \n1987:           4. **Remediation Workstreams**\n1988:              - Ordered action groups: P0 first, then P1, with P2 advisories separated\n1989: \n1990:           5. **Spec Seed**\n1991:              - Concrete seed bullets for follow-on spec updates\n1992: \n1993:           6. **Plan Seed**\n1994:              - Concrete starter tasks for `/speckit:plan`\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 1995]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml, lines 1925-1994\n1925:              - status: active | duplicate | upgraded | downgraded | contested | resolved_false_positive\n1926:              - Record first_seen, upgraded_in, previous_severity for severity changes\n1927:              - Record dimensions array reflecting all dimensions that emitted this finding\n1928:           5. Resolve contradictions:\n1929:              - Findings marked contested across iterations → referee pass\n1930:              - Determine final severity and status\n1931:           6. Count only 'active' findings for totals\n1932:         outputs:\n1933:           - finding_registry: \"Deduplicated list of all findings with metadata\"\n1934:           - active_p0: \"Count of active P0 findings\"\n1935:           - active_p1: \"Count of active P1 findings\"\n1936:           - active_p2: \"Count of active P2 findings\"\n1937: \n1938:       step_adversarial_selfcheck:\n1939:         action: \"Final adversarial self-check on all P0 and P1 findings\"\n1940:         algorithm: |\n1941:           For each active P0/P1 finding:\n1942:             1. Hunter: Re-verify finding against source code (re-read file:line)\n1943:             2. Skeptic: Challenge severity — is this really P0/P1? Could it be P2?\n1944:             3. Referee: Final call — confirm, downgrade, or mark false_positive\n1945:           Update finding_registry with adjudicated results.\n1946: \n1947:       step_emit_resource_map:\n1948:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n1949:         action: \"Emit {state_paths.resource_map_output} from converged review deltas unless config.resource_map.emit is false\"\n1950:         dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n1951:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors --emit-resource-map\"\n1952:         read:\n1953:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1954:           - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n1955:         write:\n1956:           - \"{state_paths.resource_map_output}\"\n1957:         guarantee: \"Reducer skips cleanly when config.resource_map.emit == false and writes a deterministic resource-map when enabled.\"\n1958:         note: \"A fan-out root has no root state log before closeout, so the root reducer would fail on the missing file. Each lineage emits its own map, so the report names the ones that exist at {artifact_dir}/lineages/*/resource-map.md.\"\n1959: \n1960:       step_resource_map_coverage_gate:\n1961:         action: \"If resource_map_present, compute the Resource Map Coverage Gate synthesis inputs; otherwise preserve the skip note\"\n1962:         note: \"Cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md. Report touched entries, untouched entries split into expected-by-scope vs gap, and implementation paths absent from the map. Findings raised here use category resource-map-coverage with severity calibrated to the gate outcome.\"\n1963: \n1964:       step_compile_review_report:\n1965:         action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n1966:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1967:         instructions: |\n1968:           Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n1969: \n1970:           1. **Executive Summary**\n1971:              - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n1972:              - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n1973:              - P0/P1/P2 counts (active only)\n1974:              - Review scope summary\n1975:              - Operator review focus: config.reviewFocus verbatim, or omit this line when it is null\n1976: \n1977:           2. **Planning Trigger**\n1978:              - State whether `/speckit:plan` is required\n1979:              - Include a fenced `json` block labeled `Planning Packet`\n1980:              - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n1981:              - Build `activeFindings`, `findingClasses`, and `affectedSurfacesSeed` from reducer-owned state plus iteration JSONL `findingDetails`; if a field is missing, mark it `UNKNOWN` instead of inferring it from prose\n1982: \n1983:           3. **Active Finding Registry**\n1984:              - Unified registry for active P0/P1/P2 findings\n1985:              - For each: ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints\n1986: \n1987:           4. **Remediation Workstreams**\n1988:              - Ordered action groups: P0 first, then P1, with P2 advisories separated\n1989: \n1990:           5. **Spec Seed**\n1991:              - Concrete seed bullets for follow-on spec updates\n1992: \n1993:           6. **Plan Seed**\n1994:              - Concrete starter tasks for `/speckit:plan`\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 1995]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":70,\"offset\":1925,\"path\":\".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794781463957,"end":1794781464395}}}}
