{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781508253,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","part":{"partID":"prt_1e14fe5eb001117SE22fl5OHiN","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeZfELy9ETJ0Z0Sg","messageID":"msg_1e14fccdd001pRO6xKDmIOCSj1","type":"tool","id":"call_e0ae27898c0b4698930a29e3","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Report - kill-switch-cli confirming round 5b\n\n- Lineage: `kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b` (`specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b`)\n- Run: `fanout-kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b-1794780590351-ezt1v0`\n- Area: pass-five confirming round `5b`, `kill-switch-cli`\n- Fix range: `2a1a42263cc..d21dbc1cafe`; the last commit touching any scope path is `d0f605b42f8`\n- Iterations: 3 of 3; stop reason `maxIterationsReached` (no graph-backed convergence decision exists)\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n**Verdict: PASS. hasAdvisories: true.**\n\n- Active findings: P0 = 0, P1 = 0, P2 = 2.\n- Five of the six confirmed pass-five P2 findings for this area are fixed at the file and line the verifier named; the sixth is fixed in the section it named and left one folder short in the same file.\n- One confirmed finding was fixed at only one of the two sites the pass-five iteration had named: `ENV-REFERENCE.md:74-75` now lists every alias, while `.skilled/hooks/README.md`, the table both docs call the canonical index, still omits four names the resolver honors.\n- Review scope: the five `kill-switch-cli` paths in `review-scope-5b.txt` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts`), plus the shared docs that describe them.\n- Operator review focus: Confirming round 5b of code review pass five of command surfacing. Read review/review-brief-5b.txt in the packet first and follow it. Review the files in review/review-scope-5b.txt whose area equals your lineage label without its -confirm-5b suffix, plus docs that describe them. Each finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input. Check that the shell write reader misses no in-place edit, the COMMAND reader reads only a line the model printed as its own, the arena builder refuses a dirty source, a stale build, an escaping or absolute link and answers a failed check with a JSON line, a live turn checks for a remote every turn and has no network push, the kill-switch names agree in code and docs, and docs agree with code. Never open command-prompts.jsonl, holdout-prompts.jsonl or behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl except through jq del(.prompt). Change no code and write only inside your lineage folder.\n\nWhat the round confirms, in one line each:\n\n| Confirmed pass-five finding | State at `d0f605b42f8` |\n|---|---|\n| `iter2-P2-env-alias-column` | Fixed at `ENV-REFERENCE.md:74-75`; the canonical index it points to still omits four names (P2 below) |\n| `iter2-P2-env-source-column` | Fixed: the CLI and the handler are named in the Source cell |\n| `iter2-P2-cp003-control-aliases` | Fixed: the control command unsets all ten names, which is the complete set |\n| `iter3-P2-launcher-switch-fixture` | Fixed: the fixture is derived from `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` and asserts ten entries |\n| `iter3-P2-cli-mk-alias-filter` | Fixed: all ten names run and the `MK_` reason is deliberately loose with a comment |\n| `iter3-P2-lib-readme-tree` | Fixed for section 4 (22 modules, 14 folders); section 3 still omits `skill-graph/` (P2 below) |\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\n`/speckit:plan` is **not** required to close this confirming round: the verdict is PASS with two documentation advisories, no P0 and no P1.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"triggered\": false,\n  \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n  \"hasAdvisories\": true,\n  \"activeFindings\": [\"c5b-iter1-P2-hooks-index-aliases\", \"c5b-iter1-P2-topology-skill-graph\"],\n  \"remediationWorkstreams\": [\n    {\n      \"order\": 1,\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"finding\": \"c5b-iter1-P2-hooks-index-aliases\",\n      \"action\": \"Add MK_HOOKS_DISABLED and the three MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_* names to the hook kill-switch index, or generate that table and ENV-REFERENCE from the resolver constants.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"order\": 2,\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"finding\": \"c5b-iter1-P2-topology-skill-graph\",\n      \"action\": \"Add skill-graph/ to the lib package topology between shared/ and utils/, or state that the section is a curated overview.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"specSeed\": [\n    \"The kill-switch alias inventory is a generated artifact, not four hand-edited copies.\",\n    \"A module map section states whether it is exhaustive before a missing entry becomes a defect.\"\n  ],\n  \"planSeed\": [\n    \"Generate the ENV-REFERENCE switch rows and the hooks README kill-switch index from MASTER_ALIASES and LEGACY_ALIASES, with a test that fails when a doc is short a name.\",\n    \"Add skill-graph/ to lib/README.md section 3 and a check that every folder in section 4 appears in section 3.\"\n  ],\n  \"findingClasses\": [\"class-of-bug\", \"instance-only\"],\n  \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\"hook kill-switch index\", \"ENV-REFERENCE switch table\", \"CP-003 control command\", \"lib package topology\", \"lib directory tree\"],\n  \"fixCompletenessRequired\": false\n}\n```\n\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\n\n### c5b-iter1-P2-hooks-index-aliases\n\n- Severity: P2. Dimension: traceability.\n- File: `.skilled/hooks/README.md:44` (the claim at `:36` and `:40`; the master alias is absent from the whole file).\n- Evidence: the row lists four aliases and no `MK_` name; `rg -n \"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED|MK_SKILL_ADVISOR\" .skilled/hooks/README.md` returns no hit. The resolver honors `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED` as a master alias and the three `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_*` names as legacy aliases `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:38-41,64-78]`. A read-only probe returned `reason: \"master\"` for `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED` and `reason: \"kill\"` for each of the other three. This commit added those names to `ENV-REFERENCE.md:74-75`, and `hook-flags.env.example:12-15` points at `hooks/README.md` as the canonical index. Pass-five iteration 2 named this table as the second site of the same drift `[SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/iterations/iteration-002.md:38]`.\n- Impact: the file advertised as the single source of truth under-reports the switch set by four names, including the master alias that disables every repo-authored hook. An operator reading it cannot tell that `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED=1` or `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` works.\n- Fix: add the four names, or generate both index tables from the resolver constants.\n- Disposition: active. Finding class: class-of-bug. Scope proof: four doc copies compared against `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts:74-81]`; `ENV-REFERENCE.md` and CP-003 carry all ten, `hooks/README.md` carries six of ten. Affected surface hints: [\"hook kill-switch index\", \"ENV-REFERENCE switch table\", \"CP-003 control command\", \"resolver alias constants\"].\n\n### c5b-iter1-P2-topology-skill-graph\n\n- Severity: P2. Dimension: maintainability.\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:69`.\n- Evidence: section 3 `PACKAGE TOPOLOGY` goes from `shared/` to `utils/` and never names `skill-graph/`; section 4 lists it at `:135` and the folder is in the tree at `d21dbc1cafe`. The fix added nine folders to section 4 and left section 3 one short.\n- Impact: the only section that carries a purpose line per folder drops the folder that owns the skill graph, which `tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts` imports and `lib/daemon/lease.js` uses.\n- Fix: add `skill-graph/` with a one-line purpose, or state that section 3 is curated.\n- Disposition: active. Finding class: instance-only. Scope proof: `git ls-tree` shows 14 folders and 22 modules; section 4 matches all, section 3 matches 13 of 14 folders. Affected surface hints: [\"lib package topology\", \"lib directory tree\"].\n\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n\n**P0:** none.\n\n**P1:** none.\n\n**P2 advisories, in order:**\n\n1. `c5b-iter1-P2-hooks-index-aliases` — complete the hook kill-switch index, preferably by generating it. This is the one that matters beyond polish: it is the documented inventory of a safety control.\n2. `c5b-iter1-P2-topology-skill-graph` — add one folder to the package topology, or mark the section curated.\n\n## 5. Spec Seed\n\n- A kill-switch inventory that claims completeness is generated from the resolver's alias constants; a second hand-maintained copy is a defect waiting for the next alias.\n- A topology section states whether it is exhaustive; otherwise a gap cannot be told from curation.\n\n## 6. Plan Seed\n\n- Replace the alias column in `hooks/README.md` and the two rows in `ENV-REFERENCE.md` with generated content from `MASTER_ALIASES` and `LEGACY_ALIASES`, plus a test that a doc listing fewer names than `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` fails.\n- Add `skill-graph/` to `lib/README.md` section 3 and a consistency check between sections 3 and 4.\n\n## 7. Traceability Status\n\n### Core Protocols\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| `spec_code` | pass | The ten-name set matches `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` and the resolver; the two docs now carry all ten; the two tests read the constant `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts:74-81]` `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:38-78]` |\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | No packet checklist row names this area; the confirming brief is the checklist and both of its kill-switch items are covered, with the two advisories recorded rather than passed silently |\n\n### Overlay Protocols\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | No agent definition changed in this area |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | No runtime mirror changed in this area |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | pass | CP-003's control command and the launcher/CLI fixtures checked against the resolver |\n| `playbook_capability` | pass | CP-003 unsets the complete env switch set; `DEFAULT_OFF` carries only `session-handover` `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:104-106]` |\n\n`AC_COVERAGE`: exempt. This lineage's artifact directory is a fan-out child, not a Level 2+ spec folder with a checklist and an in-progress implementation summary.\n\n## 8. Deferred Items\n\n- The `MK_` bridge and the Vibe adapter: `buildAdvisorPart` reads the same switch through an injected `isEnabled` default `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs:212-222]`. That file is the `vibe-hooks-doctor` area of this round; whether `ENV-REFERENCE.md:75` should name it as a sixth Source belongs to that lineage, not this one.\n- `manual-testing-playbook.md:209` shows the display label `003-global-disable-flag.md` while its href resolves to the real file. The label is cosmetic, the line is unchanged by the fix range, and the file is the `docs-metadata` area. Deferred to that lineage.\n- `CHILD_ENV_ALLOWLIST`'s comment about the absent disable switch sits directly above an unrelated key `[SOURCE: .skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs:159-161]`. Read as a statement about the allowlist it is accurate; recorded as a reading hazard only.\n- Confirming round `5c` is not triggered by this lineage: no P1 was confirmed and no fix commit follows from these two advisories.\n\n## Dimension Expansion Map\n\n- Review directions selected: doc-versus-code name parity (D1/D3), the launcher env trust boundary and test isolation (D2), the duplication cost of four hand-maintained alias copies and two module-map sections (D4).\n- Completed pivots: 0. Failed pivots: 0. Audited overrides: 0.\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded; the area's surfaces are all read.\n\n## 9. Search Ledger\n\n| Bug class | Disposition | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| `alias_set_drift` | confirmed (P2) | The canonical index omits four names the resolver honors |\n| `module_map_drift` | confirmed (P2) | Section 3 omits one folder section 4 and the tree have |\n| `switch_bypass` | ruled out | `DEFAULT_OFF` has one entry and it is not the advisor; the master and legacy loops cover all ten names |\n| `fixture_narrowing` | ruled out | The fixture derives from the constant and asserts ten entries before the env assertion |\n| `switch_leak` | ruled out | Exact-set child env allowlist with no switch name; the fixture asserts all ten are dropped |\n| `test_isolation` | ruled out | Per-case `mkdtemp` root and a `HOOK_FLAGS_CONFIG` that does not exist |\n| `prompt_leak` | ruled out | The three prompt files were counted only (224 / 63 / 36 rows); no reviewed file reads them |\n| `fix_provenance` | ruled out | Every scope path's last touching commit is `d0f605b42f8`, inside the range; the diff to `d21dbc1cafe` is empty |\n\nsearchDebt: none. ruledOutCandidates: all seven listed above. cleanSearchProof: every dimension's candidate bug classes were either confirmed or ruled out with cited evidence; no class was left unexamined.\n\n## 10. Audit Appendix\n\n### Convergence Summary\n\n- Iterations: 3. New findings per iteration: 2, 0, 0. Weighted new-finding ratios: 1.0, 0.0, 0.0.\n- Dimensions covered: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability (4/4).\n- Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached`. The coverage graph was unavailable in all three iterations (`graphStatus: unavailable`, `graphConvergenceScore: 0`), so no graph-backed convergence decision existed and the run does not claim `converged`.\n- Advisory self-check for P0/P1: not applicable, no P0 or P1 was raised. Both P2s were replayed unchanged in iteration 3 before counting them.\n\n### Ruled-Out Claims\n\n- The `MK_` names are only documentation: disproved by the resolver probe.\n- The fix was complete when `ENV-REFERENCE.md` changed: disproved by the canonical index it defers to.\n- The lib README fix was complete: disproved by section 3.\n- The three added `MK_` test cases share state: disproved by the per-case temp root.\n- The reviewed content is stale: disproved by the last-touching-commit check.\n\n### Sources Reviewed\n\n`review-brief-5b.txt`, `review-scope-5b.txt`, `review-focus-5b.txt`, `verify-5/report.md`, `032-review-pass-five-remediation/plan.md`, `review-core.md` (review doctrine), `ENV-REFERENCE.md`, `global-disable-flag.md`, `lib/README.md`, `launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts`, `skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts`, `skill-advisor-cli-test-utils.ts`, `hook-flags.cjs`, `env-aliases.cjs`, `advisor-disabled.ts`, `system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs`, `hooks/README.md`, `hook-flags.env.example`, `hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs` (context only), and the pass-five `kill-switch-cli-5` iterations.\n\n### Fix Provenance\n\nThe fix for this area landed at `d0f605b42f8` (`fix(system-skill-advisor): close the review pass five findings in the behaviour tooling`), which is an ancestor of `d21dbc1cafe` and of `HEAD` `9c031900e44`. `git diff --stat d0f605b42f8 d21dbc1cafe` over the five scope paths is empty, so the content reviewed here is the fix state and no later commit in the range moved it.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Report - kill-switch-cli confirming round 5b\\n\\n- Lineage: `kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b` (`specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b`)\\n- Run: `fanout-kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b-1794780590351-ezt1v0`\\n- Area: pass-five confirming round `5b`, `kill-switch-cli`\\n- Fix range: `2a1a42263cc..d21dbc1cafe`; the last commit touching any scope path is `d0f605b42f8`\\n- Iterations: 3 of 3; stop reason `maxIterationsReached` (no graph-backed convergence decision exists)\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\n**Verdict: PASS. hasAdvisories: true.**\\n\\n- Active findings: P0 = 0, P1 = 0, P2 = 2.\\n- Five of the six confirmed pass-five P2 findings for this area are fixed at the file and line the verifier named; the sixth is fixed in the section it named and left one folder short in the same file.\\n- One confirmed finding was fixed at only one of the two sites the pass-five iteration had named: `ENV-REFERENCE.md:74-75` now lists every alias, while `.skilled/hooks/README.md`, the table both docs call the canonical index, still omits four names the resolver honors.\\n- Review scope: the five `kill-switch-cli` paths in `review-scope-5b.txt` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts`), plus the shared docs that describe them.\\n- Operator review focus: Confirming round 5b of code review pass five of command surfacing. Read review/review-brief-5b.txt in the packet first and follow it. Review the files in review/review-scope-5b.txt whose area equals your lineage label without its -confirm-5b suffix, plus docs that describe them. Each finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input. Check that the shell write reader misses no in-place edit, the COMMAND reader reads only a line the model printed as its own, the arena builder refuses a dirty source, a stale build, an escaping or absolute link and answers a failed check with a JSON line, a live turn checks for a remote every turn and has no network push, the kill-switch names agree in code and docs, and docs agree with code. Never open command-prompts.jsonl, holdout-prompts.jsonl or behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl except through jq del(.prompt). Change no code and write only inside your lineage folder.\\n\\nWhat the round confirms, in one line each:\\n\\n| Confirmed pass-five finding | State at `d0f605b42f8` |\\n|---|---|\\n| `iter2-P2-env-alias-column` | Fixed at `ENV-REFERENCE.md:74-75`; the canonical index it points to still omits four names (P2 below) |\\n| `iter2-P2-env-source-column` | Fixed: the CLI and the handler are named in the Source cell |\\n| `iter2-P2-cp003-control-aliases` | Fixed: the control command unsets all ten names, which is the complete set |\\n| `iter3-P2-launcher-switch-fixture` | Fixed: the fixture is derived from `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` and asserts ten entries |\\n| `iter3-P2-cli-mk-alias-filter` | Fixed: all ten names run and the `MK_` reason is deliberately loose with a comment |\\n| `iter3-P2-lib-readme-tree` | Fixed for section 4 (22 modules, 14 folders); section 3 still omits `skill-graph/` (P2 below) |\\n\\n## 2. Planning Trigger\\n\\n`/speckit:plan` is **not** required to close this confirming round: the verdict is PASS with two documentation advisories, no P0 and no P1.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"triggered\\\": false,\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n  \\\"hasAdvisories\\\": true,\\n  \\\"activeFindings\\\": [\\\"c5b-iter1-P2-hooks-index-aliases\\\", \\\"c5b-iter1-P2-topology-skill-graph\\\"],\\n  \\\"remediationWorkstreams\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"order\\\": 1,\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"finding\\\": \\\"c5b-iter1-P2-hooks-index-aliases\\\",\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Add MK_HOOKS_DISABLED and the three MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_* names to the hook kill-switch index, or generate that table and ENV-REFERENCE from the resolver constants.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"order\\\": 2,\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"finding\\\": \\\"c5b-iter1-P2-topology-skill-graph\\\",\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Add skill-graph/ to the lib package topology between shared/ and utils/, or state that the section is a curated overview.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"specSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"The kill-switch alias inventory is a generated artifact, not four hand-edited copies.\\\",\\n    \\\"A module map section states whether it is exhaustive before a missing entry becomes a defect.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"planSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"Generate the ENV-REFERENCE switch rows and the hooks README kill-switch index from MASTER_ALIASES and LEGACY_ALIASES, with a test that fails when a doc is short a name.\\\",\\n    \\\"Add skill-graph/ to lib/README.md section 3 and a check that every folder in section 4 appears in section 3.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"findingClasses\\\": [\\\"class-of-bug\\\", \\\"instance-only\\\"],\\n  \\\"affectedSurfacesSeed\\\": [\\\"hook kill-switch index\\\", \\\"ENV-REFERENCE switch table\\\", \\\"CP-003 control command\\\", \\\"lib package topology\\\", \\\"lib directory tree\\\"],\\n  \\\"fixCompletenessRequired\\\": false\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\\n\\n### c5b-iter1-P2-hooks-index-aliases\\n\\n- Severity: P2. Dimension: traceability.\\n- File: `.skilled/hooks/README.md:44` (the claim at `:36` and `:40`; the master alias is absent from the whole file).\\n- Evidence: the row lists four aliases and no `MK_` name; `rg -n \\\"MK_HOOKS_DISABLED|MK_SKILL_ADVISOR\\\" .skilled/hooks/README.md` returns no hit. The resolver honors `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED` as a master alias and the three `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_*` names as legacy aliases `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:38-41,64-78]`. A read-only probe returned `reason: \\\"master\\\"` for `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED` and `reason: \\\"kill\\\"` for each of the other three. This commit added those names to `ENV-REFERENCE.md:74-75`, and `hook-flags.env.example:12-15` points at `hooks/README.md` as the canonical index. Pass-five iteration 2 named this table as the second site of the same drift `[SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/iterations/iteration-002.md:38]`.\\n- Impact: the file advertised as the single source of truth under-reports the switch set by four names, including the master alias that disables every repo-authored hook. An operator reading it cannot tell that `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED=1` or `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` works.\\n- Fix: add the four names, or generate both index tables from the resolver constants.\\n- Disposition: active. Finding class: class-of-bug. Scope proof: four doc copies compared against `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts:74-81]`; `ENV-REFERENCE.md` and CP-003 carry all ten, `hooks/README.md` carries six of ten. Affected surface hints: [\\\"hook kill-switch index\\\", \\\"ENV-REFERENCE switch table\\\", \\\"CP-003 control command\\\", \\\"resolver alias constants\\\"].\\n\\n### c5b-iter1-P2-topology-skill-graph\\n\\n- Severity: P2. Dimension: maintainability.\\n- File: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:69`.\\n- Evidence: section 3 `PACKAGE TOPOLOGY` goes from `shared/` to `utils/` and never names `skill-graph/`; section 4 lists it at `:135` and the folder is in the tree at `d21dbc1cafe`. The fix added nine folders to section 4 and left section 3 one short.\\n- Impact: the only section that carries a purpose line per folder drops the folder that owns the skill graph, which `tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts` imports and `lib/daemon/lease.js` uses.\\n- Fix: add `skill-graph/` with a one-line purpose, or state that section 3 is curated.\\n- Disposition: active. Finding class: instance-only. Scope proof: `git ls-tree` shows 14 folders and 22 modules; section 4 matches all, section 3 matches 13 of 14 folders. Affected surface hints: [\\\"lib package topology\\\", \\\"lib directory tree\\\"].\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\\n\\n**P0:** none.\\n\\n**P1:** none.\\n\\n**P2 advisories, in order:**\\n\\n1. `c5b-iter1-P2-hooks-index-aliases` — complete the hook kill-switch index, preferably by generating it. This is the one that matters beyond polish: it is the documented inventory of a safety control.\\n2. `c5b-iter1-P2-topology-skill-graph` — add one folder to the package topology, or mark the section curated.\\n\\n## 5. Spec Seed\\n\\n- A kill-switch inventory that claims completeness is generated from the resolver's alias constants; a second hand-maintained copy is a defect waiting for the next alias.\\n- A topology section states whether it is exhaustive; otherwise a gap cannot be told from curation.\\n\\n## 6. Plan Seed\\n\\n- Replace the alias column in `hooks/README.md` and the two rows in `ENV-REFERENCE.md` with generated content from `MASTER_ALIASES` and `LEGACY_ALIASES`, plus a test that a doc listing fewer names than `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` fails.\\n- Add `skill-graph/` to `lib/README.md` section 3 and a consistency check between sections 3 and 4.\\n\\n## 7. Traceability Status\\n\\n### Core Protocols\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `spec_code` | pass | The ten-name set matches `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` and the resolver; the two docs now carry all ten; the two tests read the constant `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts:74-81]` `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:38-78]` |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | No packet checklist row names this area; the confirming brief is the checklist and both of its kill-switch items are covered, with the two advisories recorded rather than passed silently |\\n\\n### Overlay Protocols\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | No agent definition changed in this area |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | No runtime mirror changed in this area |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | pass | CP-003's control command and the launcher/CLI fixtures checked against the resolver |\\n| `playbook_capability` | pass | CP-003 unsets the complete env switch set; `DEFAULT_OFF` carries only `session-handover` `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:104-106]` |\\n\\n`AC_COVERAGE`: exempt. This lineage's artifact directory is a fan-out child, not a Level 2+ spec folder with a checklist and an in-progress implementation summary.\\n\\n## 8. Deferred Items\\n\\n- The `MK_` bridge and the Vibe adapter: `buildAdvisorPart` reads the same switch through an injected `isEnabled` default `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs:212-222]`. That file is the `vibe-hooks-doctor` area of this round; whether `ENV-REFERENCE.md:75` should name it as a sixth Source belongs to that lineage, not this one.\\n- `manual-testing-playbook.md:209` shows the display label `003-global-disable-flag.md` while its href resolves to the real file. The label is cosmetic, the line is unchanged by the fix range, and the file is the `docs-metadata` area. Deferred to that lineage.\\n- `CHILD_ENV_ALLOWLIST`'s comment about the absent disable switch sits directly above an unrelated key `[SOURCE: .skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs:159-161]`. Read as a statement about the allowlist it is accurate; recorded as a reading hazard only.\\n- Confirming round `5c` is not triggered by this lineage: no P1 was confirmed and no fix commit follows from these two advisories.\\n\\n## Dimension Expansion Map\\n\\n- Review directions selected: doc-versus-code name parity (D1/D3), the launcher env trust boundary and test isolation (D2), the duplication cost of four hand-maintained alias copies and two module-map sections (D4).\\n- Completed pivots: 0. Failed pivots: 0. Audited overrides: 0.\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded; the area's surfaces are all read.\\n\\n## 9. Search Ledger\\n\\n| Bug class | Disposition | Rationale |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `alias_set_drift` | confirmed (P2) | The canonical index omits four names the resolver honors |\\n| `module_map_drift` | confirmed (P2) | Section 3 omits one folder section 4 and the tree have |\\n| `switch_bypass` | ruled out | `DEFAULT_OFF` has one entry and it is not the advisor; the master and legacy loops cover all ten names |\\n| `fixture_narrowing` | ruled out | The fixture derives from the constant and asserts ten entries before the env assertion |\\n| `switch_leak` | ruled out | Exact-set child env allowlist with no switch name; the fixture asserts all ten are dropped |\\n| `test_isolation` | ruled out | Per-case `mkdtemp` root and a `HOOK_FLAGS_CONFIG` that does not exist |\\n| `prompt_leak` | ruled out | The three prompt files were counted only (224 / 63 / 36 rows); no reviewed file reads them |\\n| `fix_provenance` | ruled out | Every scope path's last touching commit is `d0f605b42f8`, inside the range; the diff to `d21dbc1cafe` is empty |\\n\\nsearchDebt: none. ruledOutCandidates: all seven listed above. cleanSearchProof: every dimension's candidate bug classes were either confirmed or ruled out with cited evidence; no class was left unexamined.\\n\\n## 10. Audit Appendix\\n\\n### Convergence Summary\\n\\n- Iterations: 3. New findings per iteration: 2, 0, 0. Weighted new-finding ratios: 1.0, 0.0, 0.0.\\n- Dimensions covered: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability (4/4).\\n- Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached`. The coverage graph was unavailable in all three iterations (`graphStatus: unavailable`, `graphConvergenceScore: 0`), so no graph-backed convergence decision existed and the run does not claim `converged`.\\n- Advisory self-check for P0/P1: not applicable, no P0 or P1 was raised. Both P2s were replayed unchanged in iteration 3 before counting them.\\n\\n### Ruled-Out Claims\\n\\n- The `MK_` names are only documentation: disproved by the resolver probe.\\n- The fix was complete when `ENV-REFERENCE.md` changed: disproved by the canonical index it defers to.\\n- The lib README fix was complete: disproved by section 3.\\n- The three added `MK_` test cases share state: disproved by the per-case temp root.\\n- The reviewed content is stale: disproved by the last-touching-commit check.\\n\\n### Sources Reviewed\\n\\n`review-brief-5b.txt`, `review-scope-5b.txt`, `review-focus-5b.txt`, `verify-5/report.md`, `032-review-pass-five-remediation/plan.md`, `review-core.md` (review doctrine), `ENV-REFERENCE.md`, `global-disable-flag.md`, `lib/README.md`, `launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts`, `skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts`, `skill-advisor-cli-test-utils.ts`, `hook-flags.cjs`, `env-aliases.cjs`, `advisor-disabled.ts`, `system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs`, `hooks/README.md`, `hook-flags.env.example`, `hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs` (context only), and the pass-five `kill-switch-cli-5` iterations.\\n\\n### Fix Provenance\\n\\nThe fix for this area landed at `d0f605b42f8` (`fix(system-skill-advisor): close the review pass five findings in the behaviour tooling`), which is an ancestor of `d21dbc1cafe` and of `HEAD` `9c031900e44`. `git diff --stat d0f605b42f8 d21dbc1cafe` over the five scope paths is empty, so the content reviewed here is the fix state and no later commit in the range moved it.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794781472235,"end":1794781508253}}}}
